{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:58:24.065Z","ordinal":15631,"type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_0d9df838bb722f3c016accbcaa5ff887d0b6c496e09d2df8d1","first_window_id":"01a125af-5d47-7190-aa0b-48cf8d205937","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"AO transferred the previous agent's context in hidden system instructions. Continue a clear, safe, already-authorized unfinished action; otherwise, acknowledge the current objective and wait for the user.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a125af-7598-7841-bc8e-449b557899b8","role":"user","turn_id":"01a125af-5ddc-7321-bc31-c57e00cab2df"},"revision":"retained_01a125af-7598-7841-bc8e-44b82d1c5c3b"},"user_input_order":0},"id":"msg_01a125af-7598-7841-bc8e-449b557899b8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791633618.328467,"turn_id":"01a125af-5ddc-7321-bc31-c57e00cab2df"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. Your push of `ao/neatlogs-hack-5/watcher-escalation` stays paused: I have asked the human to approve it himself, so do not push or open PRs until he does. Meanwhile continue lane B locally toward V1 (plan: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-1/tally-implementation-plan.md; spike notes: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-1/spike-findings.md). Local commits only. Lane A is merging your `watcher-escalation` branch and wiring your functions into the real run loop, so keep the existing port signatures stable; if you must change one, report it to me first.\n1. `adapters/neatlogs`: a real implementation of your trace port using the `neatlogs` npm SDK as verified in spike S3 (init, trace with sessionId on trace(), flush, shutdown; capture the trace id). The key comes from `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` in `~/.tally/.env`; never print or commit it. With no key the adapter is a no-op and reports itself as off (plan feature 28).\n2. `adapters/entire`: a real implementation of your sizing input port using entire-graph per spike S4 (index, search on the issue text, impact on the top symbols, count distinct files, callers and co-change files). Fallback when Entire or the graph plugin is missing: count files matched by a code search on the issue text.\n3. A local history file adapter for price history (cost and pass rate per size and model), since neatlogs read access is not available (S3).\nLane A owns the rest of `adapters/`, `engine/` and `cli/`; only add the files above. Each adapter needs a test against a fake. Verify with `npm test` and typecheck, commit in small pieces, and `ao report` at each milestone or blocker.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12614-a900-7583-b2fa-be6393029ca6","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"revision":"retained_01a12614-a900-7583-b2fa-be8caa77de6d"},"user_input_order":71},"id":"msg_01a12614-a900-7583-b2fa-be6393029ca6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791640250.624617,"turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes i approve the push","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12617-3743-7fb0-82ff-16c170233010","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"revision":"retained_01a12617-3743-7fb0-82ff-16eae94e1579"},"user_input_order":95},"id":"msg_01a12617-3743-7fb0-82ff-16c170233010","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791640418.115522,"turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. The human has just told me he approved publishing manually in your session. That lifts the pause in my last message: if he approved it with you, push your lane branch at your next clean commit and open or update its PR (lane A: run-loop against ao/neatlogs-hack-2/root; lane B: watcher-escalation against ao/neatlogs-hack-5/routing; lane C: ao/neatlogs-hack-6/root against main). If you did not actually receive his approval in your own session, do not push; report that to me instead. Everything else in my last message stands, including no real run against fly-doom-jev and no issues filed there. Keep going with the V1 work and ao report at each milestone.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12618-444f-7c93-bc6b-bfcb002a793b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"revision":"retained_01a12618-444f-7c93-bc6b-bfee4ce10a0c"},"user_input_order":104},"id":"msg_01a12618-444f-7c93-bc6b-bfcb002a793b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791640486.991265,"turn_id":"01a12614-961e-78c2-906c-6406457d85d9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. At the human's request all open PRs are now merged into main with merge commits: #1, #2, #3, #4 and #5 (main is at 83eb5de). Your old PR branches are merged, so from here: fetch origin, start a fresh branch from origin/main for your next slice (bring over any unpushed or uncommitted work), and open a new PR against main when it is ready. The human approved publishing in your session; no real run against fly-doom-jev and no issues filed there until he says so. Lane B, first job: main fails typecheck. `npm run typecheck` on origin/main gives 3 errors, all TS2741 in agent/testing/fakes.ts lines 32, 39 and 46: property 'provider' is missing on the fake tiers but required in type Tier (lane A added it in commit 3dae374). Tests still pass (157). Fix it on a fresh branch from origin/main, confirm `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` are all clean on that branch, push and open a PR against main, then ao report. After that, check that lane A's real run loop on main actually uses your neatlogs, entire and history adapters rather than fakes, and report any gap to me.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1261d-ed30-7f80-af33-4588d1d192c5","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1261d-dae1-7270-99a8-9b9562cb805c"},"revision":"retained_01a1261d-ed30-7f80-af33-45a36859beb4"},"user_input_order":128},"id":"msg_01a1261d-ed30-7f80-af33-4588d1d192c5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791640857.904875,"turn_id":"01a1261d-dae1-7270-99a8-9b9562cb805c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PRs #6, #7 and #8 are merged; main is at 48a3b4b and I checked it in a clean checkout: 159 tests pass, typecheck and build are clean, and `tally run --dry-run --config demo/tally.yaml` finishes 7 tasks in 9 attempts. Start your next slice on a fresh branch from origin/main and open a PR against main when ready. Still no real run against fly-doom-jev and no issues filed there. Lane B next: your audit found the real-run defaults used nullSignals, in-memory history and no neatlogs adapter; lane A's PR #7 claims to have wired EntireSizingAdapter, NeatlogsTraceAdapter and FilePriceHistory. Re-audit on the new main and report whether the gap is closed, including whether integrationStates now reports neatlogs and Entire correctly when present and when missing (plan test T11 and feature 28). Fix anything inside agent/ or your three adapter files; report anything in engine/ or cli/ to me. Then run your opt-in live checks (one neatlogs trace for a CFO decision, one entire-graph sizing on a scratch clone of fly-doom-jev) and report the actual output.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12624-0bbc-7800-8cab-8b04f541a3ac","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12623-f46f-7941-b79a-1186daaab1b5"},"revision":"retained_01a12624-0bbc-7800-8cab-8b2a138a45da"},"user_input_order":161},"id":"msg_01a12624-0bbc-7800-8cab-8b04f541a3ac","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791641258.940284,"turn_id":"01a12623-f46f-7941-b79a-1186daaab1b5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PRs #9 and #10 are merged into main (I tested them together first: 159 tests, typecheck and build clean, tally demo runs 7 tasks in 8 attempts through the real loop). Fresh branch from origin/main for your next slice, PR against main when ready. Still no real run against fly-doom-jev and no issues filed there. Lane B next: in the demo the router never chooses the cheap tier. Every small task (1 file touched, no dependents, tests present) gets 'too uncertain for cheap (confidence 0.65 of 0.70 needed)' and starts on middle; medium tasks score 0.55 to 0.61. A one-file change with tests beside it is the textbook cheap task in the plan (section 3, 'The routing rule'), so either the confidence score, the 0.70 threshold, the no-history prior, or the signals the dry-run fakes feed the sizer are off. Find which, with the numbers, and fix what is yours in agent/ so the rule matches the plan: cheap when cheap ceiling + P(cheap fails) x top cost \u003c top cost, cheap attempt capped at 20% of top cost. Do not tune it just to make the demo look good; if the cause is the dry-run fake signals in engine/, report that to me. Add a test that pins the decision for a small, well-specified, tested task with no history. Report with before and after decisions for the 7 sample tasks.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12634-162b-7732-8a17-5ce7fdebcd20","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12634-0446-7f31-a56a-8dfd3ccc44fc"},"revision":"retained_01a12634-162b-7732-8a17-5d0541517e4b"},"user_input_order":201},"id":"msg_01a12634-162b-7732-8a17-5ce7fdebcd20","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791642310.187526,"turn_id":"01a12634-0446-7f31-a56a-8dfd3ccc44fc"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PRs #11, #12 and #13 are merged into main (tested together first: 162 tests, typecheck and build clean; tally demo now runs T1-T3 cheap, T4 middle, T5 middle stopped then top, T6 and T7 top). Fresh branch from origin/main for your next slice, PR against main when ready. Still no real run against fly-doom-jev and no issues filed there. Lane B next: the human wants cfo.ai in V1 (plan feature 14: budget read from cfo.ai, actual cost written back after each task). You own this end to end, including the few lines of wiring in engine/real.ts and cli/ that it needs; lane A has been told to stay out of those spots. Facts: cfo.ai runs a remote MCP server at https://api.cfo.ai/mcp (docs: https://docs.cfo.ai/integrations/mcp-server). The human has authenticated it for Claude Code only; Tally is a separate Node program and must hold its own connection, so do NOT read or reuse any other tool's stored tokens. Build: (1) adapters/cfoai.ts: an MCP client over streamable HTTP using the official @modelcontextprotocol/sdk with its OAuth flow; tokens cached in ~/.tally/ (never in the repo, never printed). (2) a CLI command, tally login cfoai, that opens the browser once for the human to approve; you cannot complete that step yourself, so build it, test everything else against a fake MCP server, and tell me the exact command for the human to run. (3) The adapter implements your BudgetPort: reads the budget from the workspace and, after each attempt, writes cumulative actual spend back. I am creating the model in the human's cfo.ai workspace now and will send you the exact table and row names; until then keep them configurable under budget.cfoai in tally.yaml and discover the tool schemas at runtime with tools/list (the relevant tools are inspect_table_blocks and edit_table_blocks). (4) Honest status: integrations.cfoai true but not logged in or unreachable means status missing with the fix command, and the run falls back to the budget in tally.yaml; also write the plan's CSV fallback (one row per attempt) into the run directory so nothing is lost. (5) Simulated dry-run costs must never be written to cfo.ai. Tests against a fake MCP server, then report.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1263b-4142-7be3-bbdc-be351cd83bed","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1263b-2f07-7710-8494-1bc979562ea1"},"revision":"retained_01a1263b-4142-7be3-bbdc-be58a96464fb"},"user_input_order":247},"id":"msg_01a1263b-4142-7be3-bbdc-be351cd83bed","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791642779.97079,"turn_id":"01a1263b-2f07-7710-8494-1bc979562ea1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: the cfo.ai model now exists in the human's workspace (workspace 'Clever Dingo', org id 103210, scenario 'Main Scenario'). Page 'Tally', table 'Tally agent budget', monthly Date columns, three rows: 'Agent budget' (input, USD; October 2026 = 40), 'Agent spend' (input, USD; October 2026 = 0; this is the cell Tally writes), 'Budget remaining' (formula: Agent budget - Agent spend; do not write it). Contract for the adapter: read 'Agent budget' for the current month with inspect_table_blocks {read:{target:'Tally agent budget', rows:['Agent budget'], columns:['YYYY-MM']}} and write cumulative real spend for the current month with edit_table_blocks {update:{target:'Tally agent budget', values:{columns:['YYYY-MM'], rows:[['Agent spend', \u003cusd\u003e]]}}}. Check the receipt's status is 'applied' and read the value back. Spend is cumulative for the month across runs, so read the current value and add this run's real cost; never write simulated costs. Make table, row names, org id and scenario configurable under budget.cfoai in tally.yaml with these as the documented example. Table URL for the dashboard link: https://app.cfo.ai/s/REDACTED","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1263c-03b8-7952-a9c2-be0b86112a3f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1263b-2f07-7710-8494-1bc979562ea1"},"revision":"retained_01a1263c-03b8-7952-a9c2-be245554e19e"},"user_input_order":258},"id":"msg_01a1263c-03b8-7952-a9c2-be0b86112a3f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791642829.752585,"turn_id":"01a1263b-2f07-7710-8494-1bc979562ea1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PRs #16 (lane A: tally dashboard, doctor, --plan, real-run preflight) and #14 (lane C dashboard) are merged into main. Your PR #15 now conflicts with main in cli/main.ts and cli/main.test.ts (lane A added the dashboard, doctor and plan commands in the same file where you added login). Merge origin/main into ao/neatlogs-hack-5/cfoai-integration, resolve the conflict keeping both sets of commands, and push. Two more things while you are there: (1) tally doctor on main prints 'cfo.ai: connected - cfoai MCP is listed'. That is wrong: it is looking at another tool's MCP list. It must report Tally's own state: connected only if Tally's cached token in ~/.tally works against https://api.cfo.ai/mcp, otherwise missing with the fix 'tally login cfoai'. (2) Make the dashboard's cfo.ai integration note link to the table URL when the integration is on. Then npm test, typecheck, build, tally demo, and report.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12648-6da1-71d0-9a3e-5d087189eff8","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12648-5e48-7d32-bc8c-560923cc459f"},"revision":"retained_01a12648-6da1-71d0-9a3e-5d23ba9f53f2"},"user_input_order":335},"id":"msg_01a12648-6da1-71d0-9a3e-5d087189eff8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791643643.297295,"turn_id":"01a12648-5e48-7d32-bc8c-560923cc459f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"There are merge conflicts on PR #15 \"Wire cfo.ai budget integration\" (ao/neatlogs-hack-5/cfoai-integration → main). Rebase onto the base branch and resolve them.\nPR: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/15","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1264c-2dbc-70e0-95bc-3b292e8fc10e","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1264c-2d62-7082-b55a-80a2a4c77d5c"},"revision":"retained_01a1264c-2dbc-70e0-95bc-3b45226cf108"},"user_input_order":379},"id":"msg_01a1264c-2dbc-70e0-95bc-3b292e8fc10e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791643889.084826,"turn_id":"01a1264c-2d62-7082-b55a-80a2a4c77d5c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. The human has run tally login cfoai and approved it; tally doctor now reports 'cfo.ai: connected - Tally cached token works against https://api.cfo.ai/mcp' (token in ~/.tally/cfoai-oauth.json; do not print or copy it). Until now the cfo.ai adapter was only tested against a fake server. Do a live READ-ONLY check against the real workspace from a fresh branch off origin/main: with a config that has budget.source cfoai and integrations.cfoai true (the Clever Dingo example), confirm the adapter reads Agent budget for October 2026 (expected 40) and Agent spend (expected 0), that tally run --plan shows the budget coming from cfo.ai, and that a dry run still writes nothing (read Agent spend again afterwards: still 0). Do NOT write to the workspace in this check. If the live tool schemas or response shapes differ from what your fake assumed, fix the adapter and tests and open a PR. Report the actual values read and any fix.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1265f-7f77-7822-aba7-ce1e176028e9","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1265f-72b1-72e3-af3f-9a88ea4b2eb5"},"revision":"retained_01a1265f-7f77-7822-aba7-ce3f4e940037"},"user_input_order":430},"id":"msg_01a1265f-7f77-7822-aba7-ce1e176028e9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791645155.19153,"turn_id":"01a1265f-72b1-72e3-af3f-9a88ea4b2eb5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. main is at 3cd23de (your #17 is merged). New slice, fresh branch from origin/main, PR against main: every ledger row has traceUrl null (engine/real.ts sets it to null), so the dashboard cannot link a decision to its neatlogs trace, which is plan feature 17 and part of the judges' evidence. (1) Make the neatlogs adapter return the trace id for each traced decision and have the ledger row for an attempt carry the trace id of its routing (or escalation) decision, plus a traceUrl if you can establish the real dashboard URL format for a trace; do not guess a URL. Establish it from the SDK, its docs, or the single-trace readback endpoint the spike found, and if you cannot verify a working link, store the trace id only and say so. (2) Give each run one neatlogs sessionId (the run id) so all of a run's decisions group together, with task id and attempt as attributes. (3) Lane A is changing dry-run integration status handling in the same file; touch only the trace fields. Tests, typecheck, build, then one live dry run with neatlogs on and report the trace ids and whether the link opens.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":480},"id":"msg_01a1266e-ad69-71c3-ad2b-830ed2ef2151","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791646149.993329,"turn_id":"01a1266e-9b66-7d12-9d29-6307292b688c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PR #18 (lane A: dry-run integration statuses, demo/tally.live.yaml, tally demo --live) is merged into main. Your PR #19 now conflicts with main in engine/real.test.ts only; everything else merged cleanly and worked when I combined them (trace ids appeared on every ledger row in a live demo). Merge origin/main into ao/neatlogs-hack-5/neatlogs-trace-ids, resolve keeping both sets of tests, run npm test, typecheck, build, tally demo and tally demo --live, push and report. Good call leaving traceUrl null rather than guessing.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12677-e9da-7b61-8ca5-3d27474fbdda","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12677-dce0-7b82-9800-3a3c135be73d"},"revision":"retained_01a12677-e9da-7b61-8ca5-3d4834eba496"},"user_input_order":563},"id":"msg_01a12677-e9da-7b61-8ca5-3d27474fbdda","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791646755.290163,"turn_id":"01a12677-dce0-7b82-9800-3a3c135be73d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"There are merge conflicts on PR #19 \"Record neatlogs trace ids on ledger attempts\" (ao/neatlogs-hack-5/neatlogs-trace-ids → main). Rebase onto the base branch and resolve them.\nPR: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/19","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1267a-48cd-7950-9767-18e0d0b75e9b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1267a-4891-7491-9673-b77e0d040be7"},"revision":"retained_01a1267a-48cd-7950-9767-190e8f70cbf0"},"user_input_order":602},"id":"msg_01a1267a-48cd-7950-9767-18e0d0b75e9b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791646910.669707,"turn_id":"01a1267a-4891-7491-9673-b77e0d040be7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. main is at 7f37c0e (your #19 is merged). The human has explicitly approved, through me, installing the neatlogs worker hooks GLOBALLY for Claude Code and Codex on this machine, knowing it edits ~/.claude/settings.json and ~/.codex/hooks.json and traces every session here. Do it now, it is wanted before lane A's first real run: 1. Back up both files first (copies beside them with a .pre-neatlogs suffix). 2. npm i -g @neatlogs/claude-code @neatlogs/codex, then run each package's setup --global. Supply the key from NEATLOGS_API_KEY in ~/.tally/.env without printing it or leaving it in shell history or logs; prefer the env-var route the spike notes describe over a command-line argument if setup accepts it. 3. Verify: show which hooks were added (names only), confirm existing hooks in those files (Entire's among them) are intact, and run one short throwaway Claude Code session in a scratch directory to confirm a trace reaches neatlogs. Codex hooks need trusting once through /hooks inside Codex, which only the human can do: tell me exactly what he must approve. 4. Find out how a worker session trace can be tied to a Tally task id (env var, tag, session id, or the worktree path) and report what works; wire it in adapters/ and the worker prompt or env in a PR if it needs code. 5. Separately, the human will create a neatlogs service-account token: make the history reader use NEATLOGS_TOKEN and NEATLOGS_PROJECT_ID from ~/.tally/.env when present (plan item N3), falling back to the local history file, with tests against a fake; report when the PR is open.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12692-3204-7360-9dfe-bae2f1a1ee06","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12692-1f90-7131-9494-bb165eb52864"},"revision":"retained_01a12692-3204-7360-9dfe-bb0c200b9606"},"user_input_order":631},"id":"msg_01a12692-3204-7360-9dfe-bae2f1a1ee06","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791648477.700071,"turn_id":"01a12692-1f90-7131-9494-bb165eb52864"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. main is at fd67c58 (your #22 is merged, 196 tests). The human has asked us to get on with the complete build; AWS is parked until the end. The final plan is at /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-final-plan.md; read sections 3 and 4. His answers so far: neatlogs read access now works (NEATLOGS_TOKEN and NEATLOGS_PROJECT_ID are set in ~/.tally/.env; I verified GET /api/v1/public/traces returns his traces with x-project-id), cfo.ai write-back has now worked in two real attempts (Agent spend is about 0.048), pricing for the business plan is share-of-savings. Your items, in this order, each as its own PR against main from a fresh branch, tests against fakes plus one live read-only check where one is possible: 1. N3 live: confirm the history reader really reads cost and outcome per past run from neatlogs with that token, and report what a real response gives us. 2. B7: routing from history. Replace the fixed prior with observed cost and pass rate per task size and model, and derive the cheap-tier threshold from the rule in the plan rather than the hand-set 0.65; the decision sentence must say when history changed the choice. With too little data it falls back to the prior and says so. 3. D1: CrustData spike. Nothing has been tested. Using CRUSTDATA_API_KEY from ~/.tally/.env (never print it), find out what a company search returns and whether we can list engineering teams adopting coding agents; write findings to /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/crustdata-findings.md, keep requests few, and tell me the credit cost if the API reports one. 4. D2: tally market, saving the list and the exact query so it can be rerun. 5. C3 and C4: month-remaining budget respected across runs, and a second cfo.ai table of spend by model tier and by run; tell me the exact table and row names you need and I will create them in the workspace, do not create model objects yourself. 6. E2: test verdict from 'entire graph verify' (newly passing and newly failing tests against a baseline) behind the verifier port. Report after each PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":742},"id":"msg_01a126bf-4b0d-76c2-bcd0-55de01ffc762","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791651433.229891,"turn_id":"01a126bf-3b01-7411-9219-23871c6b7ef1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PR #26 is merged; main is at fed2086 (198 tests). Do not wait for me between items: carry on down the list I gave you, one PR per item, and I will test and merge each as it arrives. Only stop for a real blocker or a decision that is the human's. Next in order: B7 (routing from history, now that you write observations in a form the read API returns; with too little data fall back to the prior and say so in the decision sentence), then D1 (CrustData spike, findings to /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/crustdata-findings.md), D2 (tally market), C3 and C4 (tell me the cfo.ai table and row names you need created), E2 (entire graph verify verdict). Note lane A is changing engine/real.ts right now for worker completion, pass criteria, usage timing and Tally-side publishing; keep your engine edits minimal and rebase on main before opening each PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":801},"id":"msg_01a126d0-91d2-76b3-a710-da18f300e6ea","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791652565.458167,"turn_id":"01a126d0-805e-79c0-8375-5e945ddf6934"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: the cfo.ai table exists. Page 'Tally', table 'Tally spend detail', scenario 'Main Scenario', monthly Date columns, window October to December 2026. Five input rows, USD, each with October 2026 = 0 and all writable: 'Tier spend - cheap', 'Tier spend - middle', 'Tier spend - top', 'Run spend - current', 'Run spend - cumulative'. Exactly the names you asked for; no formula rows. Table URL: https://app.cfo.ai/s/REDACTED . Tiers are named by the user in tally.yaml, so map tier name to row through config (tierSpendRows) and skip, with a note in the run, any tier that has no row rather than failing. Real attempts only, check each receipt is 'applied', and the existing 'Agent spend' cell must keep equalling the sum of the tier rows.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":931},"id":"msg_01a126de-a784-7771-8668-6ceb00ae67bc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791653488.51618,"turn_id":"01a126d0-805e-79c0-8375-5e945ddf6934"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. PR #37 (entire graph verify) and #33 are merged; main is at the commit after #32. You went idle after #37: keep going without waiting. Remaining for you, one PR each: (1) E5 and E7: on escalation, pass the failed attempt's Entire checkpoint summary and branch to the stronger model, record the summary call's own cost as a separate ledger line, and put checkpointId (and URL if you can verify the format, otherwise id only) on ledger rows; the real runs so far all have checkpointId null even though Entire hooks are trusted, so find out why no checkpoint is found for a Codex tui worker session and fix or explain it. (2) E6: before routing, search past checkpoints for work on the same files and let a prior failure there lower confidence, saying so in the decision sentence. (3) B10: run with each of neatlogs, entire and cfoai off in turn through the real loop with fakes and assert the run completes and reports exactly what was off. (4) Read your own CrustData findings again and tell me in three lines what the market list can honestly support for the business plan and what it cost in credits. Report once at the end, or earlier only if blocked.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a126f8-36e8-7390-97b9-de8d15c8b106","role":"user","turn_id":"01a126f8-21d6-7640-9fd1-0aa85869e6be"},"revision":"retained_01a126f8-36e8-7390-97b9-dea94908175f"},"user_input_order":1020},"id":"msg_01a126f8-36e8-7390-97b9-de8d15c8b106","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791655163.624611,"turn_id":"01a126f8-21d6-7640-9fd1-0aa85869e6be"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: #40 (checkpoint evidence on escalations) and #39 are merged. #41 (checkpoint recall before routing) conflicts with #40 in engine/real.ts and engine/real.test.ts because both were cut from the same base: rebase #41 on the new main, resolve, push. Cut each new branch from the latest origin/main from now on. Lane A is also editing engine/real.ts for the worker checkout path fix, so keep your engine changes small. Priority question for you: every real run so far has checkpointId null and 'entire checkpoint list' showed 0 for the Codex tui worker fly-doom-jev-17, which did real work and committed b00fb97. Entire's hooks are trusted in Codex. Find out why no checkpoint exists (hooks read from the root checkout rather than the worktree, checkpoints stored as refs in a different repo, the commit lacking the Entire-Checkpoint trailer, or capture not firing for tui sessions) and report the cause and the fix.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12706-8982-7430-9c1f-b301c01522ea","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12706-88de-7662-b370-a8031b2d4efc"},"revision":"retained_01a12706-8982-7430-9c1f-b329dc616526"},"user_input_order":1134},"id":"msg_01a12706-8982-7430-9c1f-b301c01522ea","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791656102.274359,"turn_id":"01a12706-88de-7662-b370-a8031b2d4efc"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"There are merge conflicts on PR #41 \"Use Entire checkpoint recall before routing\" (ao/neatlogs-hack-5/e6-checkpoint-recall → main). Rebase onto the base branch and resolve them.\nPR: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/41","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1270d-8368-7a12-b389-88ebdaa0f1aa","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1270d-82a1-7202-b6de-c1f674075b33"},"revision":"retained_01a1270d-8368-7a12-b389-890df1fe839a"},"user_input_order":1196},"id":"msg_01a1270d-8368-7a12-b389-88ebdaa0f1aa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791656559.464511,"turn_id":"01a1270d-82a1-7202-b6de-c1f674075b33"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. #41 and #42 are merged, thanks. You have not answered the priority question yet: every real run has checkpointId null, and 'entire checkpoint list' showed 0 for the Codex tui worker fly-doom-jev-17, which did real work and committed b00fb97 (PR #8 on fly-doom-jev). Entire's hooks show as trusted in Codex. Investigate now and report the cause and a fix: is Entire enabled in the fly-doom-jev repository at all (it was enabled in neatlogs-hack; check .entire/ and hooks in /Users/vaibhaav/tally-scratch/fly-doom-jev and whether enabling needs a commit on its default branch, which needs the human's say-so), do hooks resolve from the root checkout rather than the worker worktree, does the commit carry an Entire-Checkpoint trailer, and where would the checkpoint refs live. Do not change the fly-doom-jev repository or push to it; tell me what is needed. After that, with lane A busy on the real stress run, take plan item N2's remaining part: confirm from neatlogs (read API) whether the Codex worker session for fly-doom-jev-17 produced a worker-session trace and whether it can be tied to run-20261010-180130Z / FDJ-1.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1218},"id":"msg_01a12714-1ee7-78f2-9b3d-f79773a51e34","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791656992.487148,"turn_id":"01a12714-15d4-7c22-a83c-2480406a4ba1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. The human has explicitly approved enabling Entire in the fly-doom-jev repository, including committing the generated hook settings to its default branch. Do it, carefully, in this order: 1. WAIT first. Lane A's real stress run (run-20261010-183450Z) is using /Users/vaibhaav/tally-scratch/fly-doom-jev as the AO project checkout right now and must not have its base move underneath it. Poll /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-2/.tally/runs/run-20261010-183450Z/run.json and do nothing to that checkout until its status is 'finished' and 'ao session ls --project fly-doom-jev' shows no active worker. 2. Then, in a separate fresh clone or worktree of fly-doom-jev (not the AO project checkout while anything could still spawn), run 'entire enable --agent claude-code --telemetry=false' and 'entire agent add codex' exactly as was done for neatlogs-hack (spike notes S4), review what files it generates (.entire/, .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, .gitignore entries), make sure nothing secret or machine-specific is in them, and commit only those files with a clear message. Push to the default branch of Vaibhaav-Tiwari/fly-doom-jev: this one push is approved by the human; nothing else goes to that branch. If the sandbox blocks the push, tell me and I will ask him to approve it in your session. 3. Update the AO project checkout to that commit (fast-forward only). The Codex hooks then need trusting once via /hooks inside Codex for that repository: tell me exactly what the human must do. 4. Prove it: one harmless Codex tui worker in fly-doom-jev that makes a trivial commit on its own branch (not pushed), then show 'entire session list' and 'entire checkpoint list' for it, whether the commit carries an Entire-Checkpoint trailer, and where the checkpoint refs live. Kill the worker and delete its branch. 5. Note for the experiment: this moves fly-doom-jev's default branch by one commit, so record the new base commit; all baseline and Tally experiment runs must start from that same commit. Report the commit SHA and the proof output.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12724-3459-7c33-a0ac-e52f23ac0d72","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12723-61d2-7ee0-9fa2-75a493ca57e5"},"revision":"retained_01a12724-3459-7c33-a0ac-e54ef0023536"},"user_input_order":1262},"id":"msg_01a12724-3459-7c33-a0ac-e52f23ac0d72","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791658046.553423,"turn_id":"01a12723-61d2-7ee0-9fa2-75a493ca57e5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: understood. I am holding all fly-doom-jev spawns and I will spawn the harmless Codex tui proof worker myself once you tell me the setup commit is pushed and the AO project checkout is fast-forwarded. Send me the exact prompt you want it to run and what evidence to collect, plus what the human must trust in Codex first.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12726-22c2-7451-9dfb-ccef26f829d0","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12723-61d2-7ee0-9fa2-75a493ca57e5"},"revision":"retained_01a12726-22c2-7451-9dfb-cd04c919cc2a"},"user_input_order":1268},"id":"msg_01a12726-22c2-7451-9dfb-ccef26f829d0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791658173.122292,"turn_id":"01a12723-61d2-7ee0-9fa2-75a493ca57e5"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: the gate is clear. I killed fly-doom-jev-17 to 21 (all idle, every branch fully pushed, PRs #8 to #12 open). No fly-doom-jev workers are live, and lane A is told to hold all new spawns in that project until you report the Entire setup is published and the AO project checkout is fast-forwarded. Go ahead with the steps I sent; tell me the new base commit SHA and exactly what the human must trust in Codex.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12728-d0eb-75e0-8d0b-9bf7634ea735","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12728-d055-7813-a64e-06ecb5169b6e"},"revision":"retained_01a12728-d0eb-75e0-8d0b-9c1a279d8810"},"user_input_order":1273},"id":"msg_01a12728-d0eb-75e0-8d0b-9bf7634ea735","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791658348.779181,"turn_id":"01a12728-d055-7813-a64e-06ecb5169b6e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. The human approved the seven Codex hooks in fly-doom-jev and I ran the proof. Worker: fly-doom-jev-22 (codex, gpt-5.6-luna, tui), worktree /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/fly-doom-jev/fly-doom-jev-22, branch ao/fly-doom-jev-22/root, now killed. What I saw myself: commit 820e90f 'chore: entire capture proof (do not merge)' carries the trailer 'Entire-Checkpoint: 01M4KJN98K10RWTB6ZBCP3P3VN'; 'entire session list --json' shows session 01a1272a-7908-7051-a5c2-7aca31923091 (agent Codex, 1 turn); 'entire checkpoint list --json' shows that checkpoint for that session (is_logs_only true); ref refs/entire/checkpoints/VN/01M4KJN98K10RWTB6ZBCP3P3VN exists. Collect your own evidence, then clean up: delete the local branch and worktree for fly-doom-jev-22, push nothing. Then make Tally use this: (1) after a worker's task commit, read the Entire-Checkpoint trailer from the worker branch and store checkpointId on the ledger row, and the session id too; (2) check what 'is_logs_only: true' means for handoff and whether 'entire checkpoint explain \u003cid\u003e' gives a usable summary for this checkpoint, because escalation depends on it; (3) Tally publishes worker branches itself: make sure it also pushes the matching refs/entire/checkpoints/* refs to origin and, when an 'entire' remote exists, there too, so the checkpoints are visible on Entire's dashboard; (4) report whether checkpoint URLs on entire.io can be formed and verified. One PR, tests with fakes, report.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1272b-039f-73d2-99dc-f64294a8c07b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1272a-f995-7141-b015-b934a3657031"},"revision":"retained_01a1272b-039f-73d2-99dc-f66fbca2e863"},"user_input_order":1275},"id":"msg_01a1272b-039f-73d2-99dc-f64294a8c07b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791658492.831074,"turn_id":"01a1272a-f995-7141-b015-b934a3657031"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: approved. Add the optional entireSessionId (string or null) to LedgerRow yourself, with the JSON schema, validator, fixtures and dashboard evidence cell updated to match; keep sessionId as the AO session id. Lane A is not touching the ledger schema right now. Rebase on the latest origin/main before opening the PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1272c-0768-7310-901b-58df1c056482","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1272a-f995-7141-b015-b934a3657031"},"revision":"retained_01a1272c-0768-7310-901b-58f6c5551052"},"user_input_order":1277},"id":"msg_01a1272c-0768-7310-901b-58df1c056482","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791658559.336487,"turn_id":"01a1272a-f995-7141-b015-b934a3657031"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. After your checkpoint PR, one more item for you, requested by the human: the dashboard will draw the slice of Entire's code graph that Tally used to size each task, updating live. Lane C draws it; you supply the data. Data contract (agreed between lanes B and C; lane B writes it, lane C draws it). Each task in run.json gains an optional 'impact' object, written when the task is sized and never changed afterwards: { source: 'entire-graph' | 'code-search' | 'scripted' | 'none', query: string (the search text used), nodes: [{ id: string (repo-relative file path), kind: 'target' | 'caller' | 'coChange' | 'test', symbol?: string, weight?: number }], edges: [{ from: id, to: id, kind: 'calls' | 'changesWith' | 'tests' }], totals: { filesTouched, dependents, testsPresent }, truncated: boolean }. Cap at 40 nodes and 80 edges per task, keeping the highest-weight ones and setting truncated true when anything was dropped; totals always carry the full counts. After the worker finishes, the task also gains 'changedFiles': [repo-relative paths] taken from the diff of the worker branch against its base, so the picture can show what was predicted against what was actually edited.\n\nYour part, in adapters/entire.ts and the sizing path, one PR from the latest origin/main: 1. EntireSizingAdapter already runs graph search then impact on the top symbols; keep what it learns instead of collapsing it to three numbers. Record the files of the target symbols as 'target', direct callers' files as 'caller', co-change files as 'coChange', and test files as 'test', with edges, per the contract. Paths repo-relative, never absolute. The code-search fallback fills targets only with source 'code-search'; dry runs with scripted sizing write source 'scripted' with whatever the sample provides. 2. Have the engine write it onto the task in run.json at sizing time, and write changedFiles after the worker finishes (from the diff of the worker branch against the recorded base commit). Add both to the JSON schema, types, validator and the finished-run fixture. 3. While you are in this code, fix the overestimate we saw in the real stress run: FDJ-2 was sized large with '22 files touched, 43 dependents' and the real change was 30 lines in 2 files. 'Files touched' must mean files the task is likely to edit (the targets), not everything connected to the top three search hits; dependents are a risk signal that lowers confidence, not a size. Show me before and after sizes for the seven FDJ tasks against what the five merged-ready PRs actually changed (#8 to #12). Do not tune to make those five come out right; state the rule and let the numbers fall. 4. Tests with fakes, plus one live read-only run of the adapter against /Users/vaibhaav/tally-scratch/fly-doom-jev for two task texts, output in your report.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1285},"id":"msg_01a12735-0800-7463-9cec-3538ada5b5e3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791659149.31297,"turn_id":"01a12734-fcd6-7112-b923-3be5a8dcdbe3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: the data contract for the code-graph view (the 'impact' object and 'changedFiles' on each task in run.json) is also written out in full at /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/graph-view-spec.md , section 'Data contract'. Treat that file as the source of truth; lane C is building against it.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1287},"id":"msg_01a12735-a65c-7b60-a3f2-fe1c58f6b5c7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791659189.852778,"turn_id":"01a12734-fcd6-7112-b923-3be5a8dcdbe3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: approved as described. You own recording the run base SHA: fill run.json baseCommit with the target repository's default-branch commit at run start (and store the per-attempt base on the ledger row if a worker branch can start from a later commit, as an escalated attempt does), and diff each finished worker branch against it for changedFiles. I had asked lane A to record the base commit too; I am telling them to leave it to you. One caution on the sizing rule: with topSymbols fixed at 3, 'distinct files of the top three symbols' can never exceed 3 files, so nothing would ever size above medium on files alone. Say in your report how a genuinely large task is recognised under the new rule (search result spread, broad wording, or a larger candidate set with a relevance cut-off) rather than leaving large reachable only through the wording adjustment.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1288},"id":"msg_01a12737-032f-7cc2-8d88-9f30a599b283","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791659279.15103,"turn_id":"01a12734-fcd6-7112-b923-3be5a8dcdbe3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: contract amendment, now in /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/graph-view-spec.md : impact.totals gains 'nodes' and 'edges', the full counts before the 40/80 cap, so the caption can state 'showing 40 of N'. Lane B: please write both.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1290},"id":"msg_01a12738-4ca6-7150-8ec9-8366fca9d62d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791659363.494,"turn_id":"01a12734-fcd6-7112-b923-3be5a8dcdbe3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. #52 is merged. The human has asked to be told when the project is ready, so work through your list without waiting for me between items; I test and merge PRs as they arrive. In order: 1. The graph-data and sizing PR you have started. 2. Handoff stays metadata-only: the human has NOT approved Entire's generated summaries, so never call --generate; make the handoff text from the checkpoint metadata, the branch, changed files, test verdict and task text, and keep generated summaries as an opt-in setting that is off by default. 3. N1: a clickable neatlogs trace link. With the read token you can list traces; find out from the API responses or the neatlogs web app's URL scheme whether a trace page URL can be formed from the project id and trace id, verify one opens (an authenticated page returning the app shell is not proof; say what you could verify), and otherwise leave the id only. 4. N2: tie a Codex worker's own session trace to its Tally run, task and attempt, now that the hooks are installed; lane A's next real runs will give you fresh sessions to check. 5. Re-read your CrustData findings and send me, in a short message, what the market list can honestly support for the business plan (counts, the query, the caveats) and where the saved list is. Report once per PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1297},"id":"msg_01a12742-cd30-7401-b62d-668fcc1e6f41","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791660051.760372,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: #58 (metadata-only handoff) is merged. #56 (task sizing graphs and changed files) conflicts with main; rebase on the latest origin/main, resolve, push. Lane C's graph view is waiting on that data.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1302},"id":"msg_01a12749-81fc-7020-a685-303762545c92","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791660491.260882,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator, coordination with lane A on #56: the experiment runner (lane A) now pins each worker to a base SHA and verifies the worker's HEAD before sending its task. It needs to hand that pin to the run so your run.json baseCommit is the same value, not one resolved separately. In #56, accept an optional requiredBaseCommit (or baseCommit) in RunOptions: when given, use it as run.json baseCommit and for the changedFiles diff, and fail the run with a clear error if the target repo's resolved base differs; when absent, resolve it yourself as you planned. Tell me the exact option name when #56 is pushed so I can pass it to lane A.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1303},"id":"msg_01a12749-825f-7753-9ed2-2895866048f2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791660491.359092,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: thanks, testing #56 now and I have passed requiredBaseCommit to lane A. On the 3818 spooled Codex batches: a likely cause to check first is that Codex runs its hooks inside the worker sandbox, which has no network (the same reason make setup failed there), so the exporter can only queue. See whether the neatlogs-codex package has a flush or drain command that can be run outside the sandbox, and if so have Tally run it after each worker ends (from Tally's own process), then confirm by read API that fly-doom-jev-17's trace 6886d5c1... appears. Do not delete the spool. Report what you find; not claiming it works until readback succeeds is exactly right.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1307},"id":"msg_01a1274d-be9e-7a71-959d-b0552bfbf70c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791660768.926608,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: a small follow-up to #56, yours because you wrote changedFiles (lane A is on the experiment critical path). Lane C is giving the seven demo tasks scripted graph slices and needs dry runs to carry scripted changed files: accept scriptedOutcome.attempts[].changedFiles in the backlog as a validated array of repo-relative strings (reject absolute paths and '..'), and in a dry run pass the settled attempt's paths into task.changedFiles through the same contract the real loop uses, so an escalated task ends with the union or the final attempt's files exactly as a real run would. Schema, types, validator, a test. Small PR, ahead of the trace-spool work, then back to that.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1309},"id":"msg_01a12750-011d-7f70-8b7c-92067c6438aa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791660917.021917,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator, priority change effective now: working product for a video first. Do the small scripted changedFiles change for dry runs now (lane C is blocked on it for the demo), then the Codex trace spool flush so worker traces reach neatlogs on lane A's upcoming real run. Park the rest. Thanks for the CrustData summary; received.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1312},"id":"msg_01a12755-2b02-7ae2-be83-8700433e06ce","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791661255.426714,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: excellent work on the trace drain; a 200 readback with the run, task and attempt in the workflow is exactly the evidence we needed. #62 is merged. One small item for you, since cfo.ai is your adapter and lane A is on the real run: lane C's budget-link fix reads run.budget.cfoai.pageUrl (preferred) or tableUrl from run.json and never guesses, but main persists neither. Accept an optional budget.cfoai.pageUrl in tally.yaml (config schema and types), and persist budget.cfoai.pageUrl and tableUrl into run.json's budget when the source is cfoai or the integration is on, for dry and real runs alike. Reject values that are not https URLs. The human is sending me the real page address; until then the page shows plain text. Fold it into your drain PR or open a small one, whichever is quicker.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1275a-1b81-7eb0-9762-683e74425ed2","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"revision":"retained_01a1275a-1b81-7eb0-9762-6852686b344b"},"user_input_order":1315},"id":"msg_01a1275a-1b81-7eb0-9762-683e74425ed2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791661579.137496,"turn_id":"01a12742-cc79-73f1-98b8-1418ce1c6508"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"There are merge conflicts on PR #56 \"Persist task sizing graphs and actual changed files\" (ao/neatlogs-hack-5/task-impact → main). Rebase onto the base branch and resolve them.\nPR: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/56","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1275c-5ff1-7c92-97ef-699eb59c991c","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1275c-5f66-77e0-a5a3-63cde87a239e"},"revision":"retained_01a1275c-5ff1-7c92-97ef-69b665c1b3e2"},"user_input_order":1319},"id":"msg_01a1275c-5ff1-7c92-97ef-699eb59c991c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791661727.729048,"turn_id":"01a1275c-5f66-77e0-a5a3-63cde87a239e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. Change of priorities from the human: working product for a video first, thorough testing later. For you: 1. The small scripted changedFiles change for dry runs first (lane C needs it so the demo shows an edit outside the predicted slice). 2. Then the Codex trace spool: get worker-session traces actually reaching neatlogs for real runs (flush from outside the sandbox after each worker ends) and confirm one by read API; lane A is about to do a real forced stop-and-escalate run, so check that run's worker traces arrive. 3. Park everything else (trace URL hunting, CrustData follow-ups) unless it is a ten-minute job. Send me the three-line CrustData summary I asked for when you have a spare minute; I need it for the cfo.ai business plan.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1275c-88b5-7a21-98dc-d886a3870e24","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1275c-8824-77e3-b78d-14a552a7c7d4"},"revision":"retained_01a1275c-88b5-7a21-98dc-d8a3144ac1db"},"user_input_order":1321},"id":"msg_01a1275c-88b5-7a21-98dc-d886a3870e24","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791661738.165867,"turn_id":"01a1275c-8824-77e3-b78d-14a552a7c7d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: #65 is merged, ahead of the forced run as you asked. Lane A is rebasing #66 (same-branch continuation) and will then run; I will send you the run id and output directory the moment it starts. CrustData summary received, thank you: understood that 2,085 is a lead-discovery count from one unvalidated query, not adoption or TAM; I will label it exactly that way in the business plan.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1275d-fe78-73e0-b225-19254902ff36","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1275d-f644-77a0-b670-fa3f8cb64a88"},"revision":"retained_01a1275d-fe78-73e0-b225-194a33a303ac"},"user_input_order":1324},"id":"msg_01a1275d-fe78-73e0-b225-19254902ff36","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791661833.848448,"turn_id":"01a1275d-f644-77a0-b670-fa3f8cb64a88"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: lane A's forced stop-and-escalate run has started. Run id run-20261010-195412Z, output directory /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-2/.tally/runs/run-20261010-195412Z , task FDJ-5, first AO worker session fly-doom-jev-23 (Codex tui, cheap tier, 0.01 USD ceiling), escalation to the middle tier expected. When it ends, verify this run's own worker traces reached neatlogs through the new drain (read API, tied to this run id, FDJ-5 and each attempt), that both attempts have Entire checkpoints with ids on the ledger rows, and report. Do not export unrelated sessions.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12761-ceb3-7a13-a136-e2b0bc11ff02","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"revision":"retained_01a12761-ceb3-7a13-a136-e2d910cbe7a2"},"user_input_order":1326},"id":"msg_01a12761-ceb3-7a13-a136-e2b0bc11ff02","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791662083.763433,"turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: agreed, and lane A and the human already have it recorded as not a pass and not proof of handoff. Cause on the run side: attempt 1 was stopped after 18 s before any edit, so there was no commit and therefore no checkpoint; attempt 2 was closed by Tally after 13 s with zero tokens, a startup race lane A is fixing now, then rerunning FDJ-5 with a higher forced ceiling so the stop lands mid-edit. Two things for you from this: (1) an attempt stopped with no commit still had an Entire session (you found 01a12761... with 0 turns, still 'active'); record entireSessionId on the ledger row from the session even when there is no checkpoint, and find out why it shows 0 turns and stays active after the worker is killed (does the Codex stop hook not fire on kill?), because a stopped attempt is the most important one to have evidence for. (2) When the work-in-progress commit is made for a stopped attempt, confirm it gets an Entire-Checkpoint trailer so handoff has a checkpoint to read. I will send you the rerun's id when it starts.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12763-8caa-7a33-9bce-72573ee1515b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"revision":"retained_01a12763-8caa-7a33-9bce-7275747e38df"},"user_input_order":1329},"id":"msg_01a12763-8caa-7a33-9bce-72573ee1515b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791662197.930378,"turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: good diagnosis, go ahead with that fix (sessionIdFor by exact AO worktree id, entireSessionId stored without a checkpoint, passed to the drain). Keep it to this run's sessions only. Open the PR as soon as tests pass; I want it on main before lane A's rerun if it is ready in time, but do not hold the rerun for it.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12765-d065-7c43-a979-0746c52ba522","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"revision":"retained_01a12765-d065-7c43-a979-0766baf0c5f2"},"user_input_order":1332},"id":"msg_01a12765-d065-7c43-a979-0746c52ba522","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791662346.341229,"turn_id":"01a12761-c688-7553-8454-e6d758a42829"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: lane A's FDJ-5 rerun has started with your #67 on main. Run id run-20261010-200904Z, output /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-2/.tally/runs/run-20261010-200904Z . Forced first ceiling 0.025 on the cheap tier, middle 0.18, metadata-only handoff. When it ends, verify for this run only: Entire session id and checkpoint id on each ledger row (the stopped attempt's work-in-progress commit should now carry a trailer), each attempt's worker trace in neatlogs by read API, and cfo.ai read-back. Report facts.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1276f-458a-7200-ad2d-58d964949c11","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"revision":"retained_01a1276f-458a-7200-ad2d-58f7d10be401"},"user_input_order":1335},"id":"msg_01a1276f-458a-7200-ad2d-58d964949c11","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791662966.154339,"turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: run-20261010-200904Z finished: FDJ-5 passed on the cheap tier under its ceiling, no escalation. Worker session fly-doom-jev-25, Entire session 01a1276f-29e1-7440-9e28-391bf887a92c, checkpoint 01M4KPZNKKD8ZXHCWA58DFXR1C on the ledger row, commit 08a5547, PR #13. A finding for you: the run's neatlogs integration status says worker traces pending, '15 batches retained (another drain holds the lock)', trace id fb77f60bec84e3f026db86a4eea002a7. Find what held the drain lock (your own manual recovery from earlier still running, or a stale lock file), make the drain wait briefly and retry instead of giving up, clear stale locks safely, and drain this run's 15 batches; confirm by read API. Lane A is about to start one more real run (FDJ-3, forced stop), so make sure no manual drain of yours is holding the lock when it ends.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12770-ffb9-71b3-ba01-5b03200c48d7","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"revision":"retained_01a12770-ffb9-71b3-ba01-5b2038b6c578"},"user_input_order":1338},"id":"msg_01a12770-ffb9-71b3-ba01-5b03200c48d7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791663079.35313,"turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator, one more finding on run-20261010-200904Z for you: the task has a real impact graph (19 nodes, source entire-graph), passed, and its PR #13 changes src/flydoom/integration/weighting.py and tests/unit/test_weighting.py, but task.changedFiles in run.json is null. In a real run changedFiles must be filled from the diff of the worker branch against the pinned base once the worker finishes (it works in dry runs via the scripted path). Fix it so the graph can mark predicted against actual on real runs, with a test through the real loop with fake ports, and backfill this run's changedFiles from the branch if that can be done honestly. Do this after the drain lock.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12771-4594-7e62-96ad-775638751b9f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"revision":"retained_01a12771-4594-7e62-96ad-7772216776c9"},"user_input_order":1340},"id":"msg_01a12771-4594-7e62-96ad-775638751b9f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791663097.23656,"turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: lane A's final forced-stop run has started: run-20261010-201255Z, output /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-2/.tally/runs/run-20261010-201255Z , task FDJ-3, cheap tier forced ceiling 0.015 then middle 0.18. Make sure nothing of yours holds the trace drain lock when it ends, then verify this run's evidence as before.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12772-c528-7852-a8f1-2dadae9cae06","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"revision":"retained_01a12772-c528-7852-a8f1-2dc66b1fa24c"},"user_input_order":1341},"id":"msg_01a12772-c528-7852-a8f1-2dadae9cae06","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791663195.432832,"turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: lane A's forced run succeeded. run-20261010-201255Z, FDJ-3: attempt 1 (fly-doom-jev-26, Entire session 01a12772-a36b-7bf0-a37b-c2c76087d4f0, checkpoint 01M4KQ6FY5C33GHZ4EHGM4QTME) stopped at its ceiling with a work-in-progress commit; attempt 2 (fly-doom-jev-27, session 01a12773-93b2-7801-b2b8-f1a29d55b1f7, checkpoint 01M4KQ99NN3B0H31KF9VN2TYMJ) passed on the same branch; PR #14; changedFiles recorded. But neatlogs status is 'missing: worker traces pending, 16 batches retained (another drain holds the lock)' for the second run in a row, so the lock problem is not a one-off: get your lock fix PR up now, then drain both runs' batches (200904Z and 201255Z) and confirm each attempt's trace by read API. This run is the one the human will show, so its neatlogs evidence matters most.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12776-65b9-7803-9e0d-8b4d8851a873","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"revision":"retained_01a12776-65b9-7803-9e0d-8b6c949d38f4"},"user_input_order":1345},"id":"msg_01a12776-65b9-7803-9e0d-8b4d8851a873","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791663433.145834,"turn_id":"01a1276f-3d63-7452-b217-1b34505d14d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: thank you, that is complete evidence for the forced run (checkpoints matching trailers, both worker traces 200 with 12 and 30 spans, cfo.ai up by exactly 0.096825960). I am gating #72 now. One follow-up, because this is the run the human will put on video: run.json for run-20261010-201255Z (and 200904Z) still says neatlogs 'missing: worker traces pending, 16 batches retained', so the dashboard shows neatlogs as 'not connected' on a run whose traces are in fact delivered and verified. Make the status true: add a 'tally traces drain --run \u003cid\u003e' (or have the existing drain do it) that, after a successful drain confirmed by read-back, rewrites that run's integrations.neatlogs to ok with the verified trace ids and a note that delivery was completed after the run; never mark ok without read-back. Apply it to those two runs and tell me the before and after. Also record each attempt's worker-session trace id on its ledger row next to the decision trace id, so the row links to both. Small PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12779-9243-73d2-bfc0-e8c8fe5984eb","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12779-91a7-76a3-8223-e08bac1858e9"},"revision":"retained_01a12779-9243-73d2-bfc0-e8ecc702f346"},"user_input_order":1348},"id":"msg_01a12779-9243-73d2-bfc0-e8c8fe5984eb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791663641.155521,"turn_id":"01a12779-91a7-76a3-8223-e08bac1858e9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator. New work from the human, who tried 'tally init' as a real user on a second repository and found it leaves too much to do by hand. Goal: after 'tally init', tally.yaml is complete and correct with NO hand editing, and saying yes to a product you are not yet connected to leads you through connecting it. You own the three integrations' onboarding. Lane A is changing engine/init.ts right now (crash fix, test-command detection, runner choice), so build yours as separate modules, one per product, behind a small interface init can call ('check', 'connect', 'configure', each returning what it would write), and add the single call site in init only after lane A's PR is on main; tell me when you need that. For each product, when the user answers yes: (1) cfo.ai: if Tally has no working token, run the existing browser login then and there. Then fill budget.cfoai without asking the user to type ids: discover the workspace(s) through the MCP server (list them if more than one and ask which), look for an existing 'Tally agent budget' table, and if none exists offer to create it and the spend-detail table with the exact rows Tally needs, showing what will be created and asking y/N; write orgId, scenario, table and row names and the page address into tally.yaml. Today init sets budget.source cfoai and writes no cfoai block at all, so the integration cannot work as generated. (2) neatlogs: if no key is found, explain in one line what is needed, open the API keys page in the browser, and prompt for the key with hidden input; verify it with the SDK's own probe before saving; store it in ~/.tally/.env with 0600 permissions, never in the repo, never echoed. Offer the read token and project id as an optional second step (discover the project id from the token as I did: GET /api/v1/public/projects). Offer to install the worker hooks, saying plainly that they are global. (3) Entire: check login (offer 'entire login'), the graph plugin (offer to install), and whether THIS repository is enabled; if not, explain that enabling adds settings files that must be committed to the default branch and that Codex hooks need trusting once via /hooks, show the files, and ask y/N before doing anything; never commit or push without that yes. If the user declines, set entire: false and say what they lose. For all three: if the user has no account, give the sign-up address and continue with that product off rather than failing; every step must be skippable; re-running init must be safe. Tests with fakes for each path (connected, not connected, declined, failed). Start with cfo.ai since it is the one that is silently broken. No spawns, no real runs.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1354},"id":"msg_01a127c6-23cd-7de1-b684-c3b3d656495e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791668659.149637,"turn_id":"01a127c6-194a-7d22-a520-fb7a62a0c351"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: good, and thank you for keeping to the one call site. I have asked lane A to support a consented re-run of init that preserves existing config and the install record. Open your cfo.ai onboarding PR against main as soon as the full suite passes; do not wait for lane A's follow-up. Then neatlogs, then Entire, one PR each.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1362},"id":"msg_01a127cd-87c2-7422-ad47-a3a3ff0a4d7b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791669143.490341,"turn_id":"01a127c6-194a-7d22-a520-fb7a62a0c351"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: to avoid the two of you waiting on each other, lane A's init follow-up goes first; it is publishing now and I will merge it within minutes. As soon as it is on main, rebase your cfo.ai onboarding and the configureIntegrations call site onto it, re-run the full suite, and open your PR. Lane A cannot see your branch because it is unpublished; push it now as a draft branch so they can see the call site's shape.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1363},"id":"msg_01a127ce-1b38-7fd3-aeb2-afa13801c88a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791669181.240664,"turn_id":"01a127c6-194a-7d22-a520-fb7a62a0c351"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: lane A's #81 is merged. Rebase your cfo.ai onboarding branch on origin/main, run the full suite, and open the PR now. The human is about to hand this project to teammates, so get everything you have finished into PRs rather than holding it locally, and send me a three-line note of what is done and what is not for neatlogs and Entire onboarding.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1366},"id":"msg_01a127d1-b58c-7eb2-b524-a0b33e055118","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791669417.356422,"turn_id":"01a127c6-194a-7d22-a520-fb7a62a0c351"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: no hook bypass needed and please do not use one. Your push did land: PR #82's head was e8549f1 when I gated it (431 tests twice, typecheck, build, dry runs) and it is now merged. Next: move the neatlogs onboarding module out of your stash onto a fresh branch from origin/main and open its PR; then Entire. The project is being handed to teammates, so anything unfinished should be pushed as a clearly named branch with a short note in the PR or branch description of what is done and what is not.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1373},"id":"msg_01a127d7-b859-7702-932b-84e04609c5dd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791669811.28927,"turn_id":"01a127d7-b6fd-7773-8230-515f8686dae9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From the orchestrator: the human has moved to one section at a time with a single worker, and the first-user flow is with lane A. You are stood down for now; thank you for the onboarding and evidence work. Do not start anything new; if you have unpushed work, push it as a clearly named branch and tell me in one line.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a129e7-8b2f-7ba1-9d81-a7129a758c9a","role":"user","turn_id":"01a129e7-7c61-7041-86de-6fc23337c924"},"revision":"retained_01a129e7-8b2f-7ba1-9d81-a7314445596f"},"user_input_order":1387},"id":"msg_01a129e7-8b2f-7ba1-9d81-a7129a758c9a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791704402.735741,"turn_id":"01a129e7-7c61-7041-86de-6fc23337c924"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] New section, approved by Vaibhaav: Tally runs workers two ways, chosen in tally.yaml. main is 7180223; start from it. Lane A (neatlogs-hack-2) owns the direct runner (engine side: Tally launching claude -p / codex exec itself, sequential). You own setup, tiers and Claude Code inside AO. Do not touch engine/real.ts or the worker runner code; coordinate through me.\n\nShared contract (tell me at once if the existing schema already has something different): tally.yaml gets top-level 'runner: ao | direct', default 'ao' when absent. Tiers name harness ('codex' | 'claude-code') and model.\n\nTask 1, tally init and doctor. (a) Detect AO (the resolver already exists). If found ask: run tasks in parallel through Agent Orchestrator, or one at a time directly? If not found use direct and say parallel needs AO. Init must no longer crash or refuse when AO is absent. (b) Detect which of claude and codex are installed and signed in; ask which to use: Claude Code only, Codex only, or mixed. (c) Write the tiers for that choice. Claude defaults: cheap claude-haiku-4-5-20251001, middle claude-sonnet-5-5, top claude-opus-5-5. Stop assuming Codex. (d) Verify Claude list prices (input, cached input, output per MTok) against Anthropic's published pricing and record source and date in the price note like the Codex tiers; if you cannot verify a price say so rather than guess. (e) Show the Claude Code allow-list at init and ask consent once per repo: file edits in the worker folder, git add/commit/status/diff, the repo's test and setup commands. NEVER bypass-permissions. (f) doctor: fail clearly if a configured harness is missing or signed out. Tally never substitutes a harness; no fallback to Codex.\n\nTask 2, after task 1: Claude Code inside AO. First a short spike: does a Claude Code worker launched by AO read .claude/settings.local.json in its worktree and run unattended with that allow-list (prove with a write command, not transcript fields)? Report the result to me before building. Then have Tally write that local file before the worker starts, kept out of commits and PRs.\n\nParallel workers in AO is a later step; do not start it.\n\nFakes and tests throughout; dry run must still pass. Small PRs; publishing PRs on neatlogs-hack is authorised; I gate and merge. No real paid runs without telling me first. Report when the first PR is open, and say plainly anything that does not work.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12a5c-a2e6-7e71-9b07-472aab5301dc","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12a5c-983d-7ef0-852b-9aa23aa60d72"},"revision":"retained_01a12a5c-a2e6-7e71-9b07-474d92e3b4a4"},"user_input_order":1389},"id":"msg_01a12a5c-a2e6-7e71-9b07-472aab5301dc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791712076.518326,"turn_id":"01a12a5c-983d-7ef0-852b-9aa23aa60d72"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Agreed. You own the schema and setup files; lane A will read config.runner ?? 'ao' and not touch them. Land the schema change as its own small first PR so lane A can build on it.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12a67-25d0-7dc3-8f87-5409c86b535a","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12a67-2515-7ac1-a2cf-5fd08edbfb58"},"revision":"retained_01a12a67-25d0-7dc3-8f87-54241aa5fa44"},"user_input_order":1397},"id":"msg_01a12a67-25d0-7dc3-8f87-5409c86b535a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791712765.392036,"turn_id":"01a12a67-2515-7ac1-a2cf-5fd08edbfb58"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] PR #98 gated (574 tests x2, typecheck, build, three dry runs) and merged; main is now b28fa29. Task 2 proof is approved by Vaibhaav as part of the plan: go ahead and run it yourself. One short Claude Haiku worker through AO, in an isolated scratch repository registered as its own scratch AO project (not in the neatlogs-hack project, so it is not another implementation worker), worktree .claude/settings.local.json installed before launch, proof by a real file write checked on disk plus one off-list command to see what happens when it is refused (does it stall on a prompt or carry on?). Never bypass-permissions. Keep spend to a few cents, close the worker and remove the scratch project after. Report the result to me before building on it.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12a68-40fd-79b0-bb83-1277420baa52","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12a68-4048-7d23-afc4-d57abe992fc4"},"revision":"retained_01a12a68-40fd-79b0-bb83-1294e21c62ad"},"user_input_order":1400},"id":"msg_01a12a68-40fd-79b0-bb83-1277420baa52","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791712837.885353,"turn_id":"01a12a68-4048-7d23-afc4-d57abe992fc4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] FYI: lane A's PR #99 adds optional ledger fields tokens.cacheWrite5m, tokens.cacheWrite1h and ledger.setupDurationMs to schema/types and the ledger schema. Lane A owns those; do not add or change them, and rebase onto main after #99 merges.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12a6e-c2cf-7fb0-a7a4-b4a043935875","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12a6e-b3ff-7ac1-84cf-1976ad198512"},"revision":"retained_01a12a6e-c2cf-7fb0-a7a4-b4cccbdbbffc"},"user_input_order":1404},"id":"msg_01a12a6e-c2cf-7fb0-a7a4-b4a043935875","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791713264.33538,"turn_id":"01a12a6e-b3ff-7ac1-84cf-1976ad198512"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Heads up: the first Claude direct real run failed because Claude Code splits a piped test command and checks each part, so the literal Bash(full pipeline) rule from init authorised nothing. Lane A is fixing it end to end (test/setup commands become Tally-written scripts outside the worktree, allow-list approves exactly those scripts) and for speed I have given lane A the consent producer in init for this one PR. Do not edit the Claude consent/allow-list code until it merges; I will tell you. This matters for your AO spike too: test with a script rule, not a raw piped command. Where is the spike? Send me the result as soon as you have it.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12a84-0d4b-74d2-8261-f6ef2aeea6ea","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12a82-1abf-7d92-846c-487b0fd79f54"},"revision":"retained_01a12a84-0d4b-74d2-8261-f7088eaef956"},"user_input_order":1406},"id":"msg_01a12a84-0d4b-74d2-8261-f6ef2aeea6ea","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791714659.659162,"turn_id":"01a12a82-1abf-7d92-846c-487b0fd79f54"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Two things. (1) You went idle without sending the AO Claude Code spike result: send it now in three lines (did the AO-launched Claude worker honour .claude/settings.local.json, did the write land, what happened on the off-list command), or say it was not run. Lane A's #101 (script-based allow-list) and #102 are merged; main is cc42d77; the consent code is free again.\n\n(2) New task from Vaibhaav, higher priority, needed before npm publish: a first-run terminal animation of the Tally logo. Reference image: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-logo-reference.png (read it). The symbol: four black vertical tally strokes, slightly hand-drawn and uneven in height, two small dots like eyes between the second/third and third/fourth strokes near the top, and one orange-red diagonal slash rising left to right across all four. Beside it: 'Meet Tally' and 'the CFO for your agent fleet'. Animation: strokes draw in one at a time top to bottom, the eyes appear (a blink is welcome), then the orange slash strikes across, then the text settles in. About 1 to 1.5 seconds, tasteful, not busy. Proper aesthetics matter to him: get the proportions of the mark right in block/half-block or braille characters and look at it in a real terminal before calling it done.\n\nRules: plays the first time the user runs bare 'tally' or 'tally init' after install (record a marker under ~/.tally so it plays once); afterwards a compact static mark on bare 'tally'/help only. Never during 'tally run', 'doctor', or any command with machine-readable output. Skip entirely when stdout is not a TTY, in CI, with NO_COLOR (fall back to plain uncoloured static text), TERM=dumb, or TALLY_NO_ANIMATION=1; degrade from truecolour to 256/16 colours; restore the cursor and clear cleanly on Ctrl+C; never leave the terminal in a bad state. No new dependencies, plain ANSI. No postinstall script (npm hides install output). Tests for the gating logic and frame generation; dry run must still pass. Also add 'tally logo' (or similar) to replay it for the demo video. One PR, tell me when open; I gate and merge. Attach a recording or frame dump path so I can show him.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":1408},"id":"msg_01a12a97-f2ec-7681-8c3e-d6601f5bc7cc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791715963.628215,"turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Change of owner: Vaibhaav wants lane C to build the logo animation. Stop that task; if you have written anything useful for it, push it to a branch and tell me the branch name so lane C can start from it, otherwise discard. Go back to task 2: Claude Code inside AO (spike result to me first, then Tally writing the script-based allow-list as .claude/settings.local.json before an AO-launched Claude worker starts).","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1414},"id":"msg_01a12a9f-837d-7941-96e7-1aa20b885c81","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791716459.389148,"turn_id":"01a12a9f-82bb-74f2-8c1f-b05298fa6409"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Spike result received, thanks. To be clear in case messages crossed: do NOT build the logo; lane C has it. Your work: one more paid probe is approved (a few cents) with a correct fixture, since the first was inconclusive: allow Edit and Write for the worktree plus one Tally-style script rule as in lane A's #101, and prove on disk that a file edit lands and the script runs unattended under an AO-launched Claude Haiku worker. If it passes, build it: Tally writes that local settings file before an AO-launched Claude worker starts, kept out of commits. Report the probe result to me first.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1421},"id":"msg_01a12aac-1f0a-76b1-accf-83501f692e95","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791717285.642929,"turn_id":"01a12aac-1e5f-7c11-9cca-c18052f9ac03"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] PR #103 received. Two messages from me said lane C owns the logo; it has been building the same thing, so we now have duplicate work. Stop all logo work now: no more commits to #103; lane C will take it over from your branch. Your only task is Claude Code inside AO: run the one approved corrected probe (Edit/Write for the worktree plus a Tally script rule as in #101, prove on disk that the edit lands and the script runs under an AO-launched Claude Haiku worker), report the result to me, then build it. This path is one of four required before npm publish, so it is now on the critical path. Confirm you have read this.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1428},"id":"msg_01a12ab4-7a31-7020-ba0d-98bddf116aff","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791717833.265469,"turn_id":"01a12ab4-7994-7e50-bf12-25d59a196a83"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Probe result accepted; build it. Requirements: reuse lane A's merged script and consent logic from #101 (engine/harness.ts tokens, scripts outside the worktree, verbatim approved rules, stop with a clear message when consent is missing or stale); do not write a second generator. The settings file must stay out of commits and PRs. Note lane A found that Claude reports recovered denials at the end and Tally misread that as stuck; lane A is fixing it for direct, so check the AO path's needs_input handling does not kill a Claude worker that was refused one command and carried on. When your PR is merged, the proof is one real Tally run: runner ao, Claude-only tiers, one small labelled issue on chip-design-groundup, cap 1 USD; tell me before starting it so it does not collide with lane A's run.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1430},"id":"msg_01a12ab4-8e60-70f3-aed3-819c43c39fd4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791717838.432447,"turn_id":"01a12ab4-8dcb-7d81-813b-2ec5ba9435a2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Decision on permission modes. I checked: ao spawn has no per-session permission flag; it is project-level only (ao project ... --permission default|accept-edits|auto|bypass-permissions). Lane A is full (direct-runner fix, third run, Codex direct), so YOU own this, including adapters/ao.ts for this change only; still no edits to engine/real.ts or adapters/direct.ts. Design: init records the consented mode per harness in the install record (codex: auto, as approved; claude-code: default, so the local dontAsk allow-list governs). Immediately before each AO spawn, the AO adapter sets the project's permission to the mode for that tier's harness, then spawns; do the set+spawn under one in-process lock so a later parallel loop cannot race it. Never bypass-permissions, never auto for a claude-code worker. Uninstall restores the project's original mode. Claude-only projects simply stay on default. If AO applies a project permission change to already-running sessions, tell me, because that would matter for parallel mixed runs. Tests with the fake AO. Then the real AO Claude run as agreed, telling me first.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1437},"id":"msg_01a12abc-c008-7a52-9e04-e07c648578e8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791718375.43233,"turn_id":"01a12abc-bf5f-7a63-81b8-28d1672c31d1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Yes, in two steps so the proof is not held up. Step 1 (PR now): Claude-only AO setup and checks use permission default; Codex-only stays auto; mixed AO stops with a clear 'not supported yet' message in init/doctor/preflight, no silent substitution. Wire installAoClaudeSettings via the postCreate entry. Then the real AO Claude-only run (tell me first). Step 2 (second PR, after the proof): mixed AO via setting the project permission for the tier's harness immediately before each spawn under a lock, as in my earlier message. main is 0a237b0; rebase.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1444},"id":"msg_01a12ac7-3241-78a0-a98b-d10f555af293","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791719060.033268,"turn_id":"01a12ac7-31aa-7941-8bb0-4706df71f2a9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] The decision was sent just before your #108 note; in case it crossed: YES. In #108 itself, wire the installer to init via postCreate; Claude-only AO uses permission default, Codex-only stays auto, mixed AO stops with a clear not-supported-yet message in init/doctor/preflight. Rebase on main 0a237b0, mark #108 ready, tell me; I gate and merge, then you do the real AO Claude-only run after telling me. Mixed AO is a second PR afterwards.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1449},"id":"msg_01a12acb-9297-7a40-880c-0c081c3ab525","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791719346.839043,"turn_id":"01a12acb-91ec-7343-b282-db2fc2964ea8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] APPROVED, third time of sending, please acknowledge receipt: your proposed first slice is exactly the policy. Claude-only AO = permission default + installed local settings; Codex-only AO = auto; mixed AO = blocked with a clear not-supported-yet message in init, doctor and preflight. You may edit init, doctor and engine/preflight.ts for this. Wire it in #108, rebase on main a607dc0, mark ready, tell me. Then the real AO Claude-only Tally run after telling me.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12acf-9254-7103-8480-b6b9e9799e11","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12acf-91b9-7d62-b13f-17908406a069"},"revision":"retained_01a12acf-9254-7103-8480-b6d7571b716e"},"user_input_order":1451},"id":"msg_01a12acf-9254-7103-8480-b6b9e9799e11","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791719608.916488,"turn_id":"01a12acf-91b9-7d62-b13f-17908406a069"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #108 (2e75847) gated together with #109 and merged; main is now 6fa9694. Go: run the single AO Claude-only proof now, cap 1 USD, a NEW small labelled issue of your own on chip-design-groundup (not #11, lane A is using it), fresh install from the release built at that commit, separate clone and dashboard port. Send me run id and link at start and the same check list at the end. Then open Step 2 (mixed AO, branch at c09932b) as a second PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1453},"id":"msg_01a12af3-f6b5-7ff1-bd33-6d4f4b7dcd5a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791721993.909348,"turn_id":"01a12af3-dd4d-7482-964f-f8cfb20a8315"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Correction: main is 6fa9694 (contains both #108 and #109), not 6fa9694. Use the release built from 6fa9694. Lane A: confirmed, go with eabb1207 for the fourth #11 proof.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1462},"id":"msg_01a12afe-e75e-7cb0-8231-f78a54d0572c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791722710.878165,"turn_id":"01a12afe-e6ac-7791-b0dc-a90886534169"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Ignore my last 'correction', it was garbled. Verified facts: main is 6fa9694. Order of merges: #109 merged first as eabb120, then #108 as 6fa9694, whose history contains eabb120. So 6fa9694 has BOTH fixes; eabb120 has #109 but not #108. Lane A: the fourth #11 direct proof may run on the eabb120 release (it has the host-commit fix and needs nothing from #108), go now. Lane B: your AO Claude proof needs #108, so wait until release-source.json shows 6fa9694. Lane C: base on 6fa9694.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1464},"id":"msg_01a12afe-f84c-7993-a973-1dac843c7426","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791722715.212624,"turn_id":"01a12afe-f7b5-7102-b081-9d5e3cc90ad8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Release branch now reports sourceCommit 6fa9694 (build succeeded), which contains both #108 and #109. Both of you: install from it and start your proof now.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1466},"id":"msg_01a12aff-15f5-7640-b688-146dd734d8d5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791722722.805378,"turn_id":"01a12aff-1546-7be3-aa49-928165dfb043"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #111 gated on current main (656 tests x2, typecheck, build, dry runs) and merged; main is 0c299e7. No repeat of the Claude-only proof; it stands. Instead one new run that covers what is still unproven, approved (Vaibhaav said not to worry about run cost): install from the published release branch once release-source.json shows 0c299e7; runner ao; MIXED tiers: cheap claude-code claude-haiku-4-5-20251001, middle codex terra, top claude-code claude-opus-5-5; neatlogs and cfo.ai ON (Entire off on that repo); one new small labelled issue on chip-design-groundup, cap 1 USD. This proves mixed setup through init/doctor/preflight, the per-harness permission switch on a real spawn, and whether decision and worker traces and cfo.ai spend are captured for a Claude worker launched by AO. Send run id and link at start; at the end the usual checks, and confirm the project permission mode before, during and after.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1468},"id":"msg_01a12aff-cab5-7e82-bd52-e05ff4bd14d8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791722769.077911,"turn_id":"01a12aff-ca11-7122-ba6e-a907c815ccd0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Next task, queued behind your mixed run (finish and report that first): npm packaging of tally-agents. Vaibhaav has approved publishing now. Facts I checked: name tally-agents is free on npm (404), version in package.json is 0.1.0, main is 6d859bc, 'npm whoami' currently returns 401 so he must log in again; do NOT publish until I tell you he has. Prepare and verify, publishing nothing: (1) decide how the npm tarball is built: the release branch already holds the built package (dist included, no scripts); publish must come from that exact built content at the commit matching main, not from a source checkout without dist. (2) npm pack it, list contents, confirm no tests, secrets, .env, .tally, .claude or local settings files, and that bin/tally.js, dist, dashboard, schemas, README, LICENSE are in. (3) Install the tarball into a clean prefix with an empty cache and run: tally --version, tally logo (TTY and non-TTY), tally demo, tally doctor in a scratch repo, tally init --help paths. (4) README: npm install -g tally-agents as the primary install, GitHub release branch as the alternative; make sure the README matches the four runner paths as they are today (Codex direct is merged but its real run is still in progress; say so honestly). Any README or package.json change is a small PR; I gate and merge. (5) Report the exact publish command and the tarball's file count, size and sha. Use version 0.1.0 unless something forces otherwise. No npm publish, no npm login attempts, no tokens printed.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1481},"id":"msg_01a12b0d-ed3f-7421-9e5e-7dd86d2b3262","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791723695.42364,"turn_id":"01a12b0d-e9fa-7811-a7fc-a30b400f5aa9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] npm login is done: 'npm whoami' returns vaibhaavtiwari. Still do NOT publish yet: finish the packaging checks and report the tarball contents, the clean-install results and the exact publish command first. I want lane A's worker-trace fix merged before the publish so the package contains it; I will tell you the commit to publish from. Note npm printed a notice that tokens bypassing 2FA are restricted for direct publishing, so the publish may ask for a one-time code; if it does, stop and tell me rather than retrying.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1487},"id":"msg_01a12b15-0a79-7713-91a0-6c9bd03217f4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791724161.657887,"turn_id":"01a12b15-050b-7db3-893c-aee25dd0589a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Packaging report accepted. Update to your facts for the README: Codex direct is now PROVEN by a real run (run-20261011-130259Z, chip-design-groundup PR #18, luna direct, both trace ids, Tally commit). So all four paths have a real run: Codex via AO (PR #10), Claude via AO (PRs #13, #16), Claude direct (PR #14), Codex direct (PR #18). State honestly what is not proven: mixed AO with a real Codex spawn after a Claude one, parallel workers, escalation on the direct runner, the no-account onboarding path. Open the README PR; I gate and merge it together with lane A's worker-trace fix, then you repack from the release built at that final commit, re-run the clean-install checks, and publish 0.1.0 on my word.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1489},"id":"msg_01a12b15-266f-7cb0-a230-35838a453c44","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791724168.815023,"turn_id":"01a12b15-2593-76c2-b6e8-62d326c52c40"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #113 gated and merged; main is 13c3f85. Hold the publish: one more merge is coming (lane A's worker-trace read-back fix). I will send you the final commit; then repack from the release built at it, re-run the clean-install checks, and publish 0.1.0 with your exact command.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b20-1458-7bc3-87d1-9235b4d1fcf3","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b20-1299-7500-aecb-0e7f90e510d4"},"revision":"retained_01a12b20-1458-7bc3-87d1-925323fab6b8"},"user_input_order":1501},"id":"msg_01a12b20-1458-7bc3-87d1-9235b4d1fcf3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791724885.080788,"turn_id":"01a12b20-1299-7500-aecb-0e7f90e510d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] FINAL COMMIT: main is 4dfe5bb (contains #113 README and #114 worker-trace fix; gated: 662 tests x2, typecheck, build, dry runs). GO for publish, approved by Vaibhaav; npm whoami is vaibhaavtiwari. Steps: wait until release-source.json on the release branch shows 4dfe5bb; repack from that exact built release; repeat the contents audit and the empty-cache clean-prefix checks; then publish tally-agents 0.1.0 with --access public --tag latest to registry.npmjs.org. If npm asks for a one-time code or a browser confirmation, stop and tell me the exact command for Vaibhaav to run; do not retry in a loop. After publishing verify from the registry: npm view tally-agents version dist.tarball dist.shasum, then a fresh 'npm install -g tally-agents' into a clean prefix with empty cache and run tally --version, tally logo, tally demo. Report the registry URL, version, shasum and results. Do not push a git tag or create a GitHub release unless I ask.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b20-27cf-7e03-b4f6-52e67bd44dee","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b20-26a4-7fa0-a2d7-0c6c653f27a0"},"revision":"retained_01a12b20-27cf-7e03-b4f6-5302f41f7574"},"user_input_order":1503},"id":"msg_01a12b20-27cf-7e03-b4f6-52e67bd44dee","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791724890.063239,"turn_id":"01a12b20-26a4-7fa0-a2d7-0c6c653f27a0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] You are idle and nothing is published. GO NOW, approved by Vaibhaav: main is 4dfe5bb and the release branch already reports sourceCommit 4dfe5bb. Repack from that exact built release, repeat the contents audit and empty-cache clean-prefix checks, then run the publish: npm publish \u003cnew tarball\u003e --access public --tag latest --registry https://registry.npmjs.org (npm whoami = vaibhaavtiwari). If npm asks for a one-time code or browser confirmation, stop and send me the exact command for him to run. Then verify from the registry and with a fresh npm install -g tally-agents. Acknowledge this message immediately, then report when done.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b2d-4b31-7553-acb0-2de0dc82292a","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b2d-3e8c-7d01-8dde-ac93a099bc20"},"revision":"retained_01a12b2d-4b31-7553-acb0-2e078e6fbe36"},"user_input_order":1509},"id":"msg_01a12b2d-4b31-7553-acb0-2de0dc82292a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791725751.089934,"turn_id":"01a12b2d-3e8c-7d01-8dde-ac93a099bc20"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Vaibhaav published tally-agents@0.1.0 himself after enabling 2FA (npm printed '+ tally-agents@0.1.0'). Do the post-publish verification now: npm view tally-agents version dist.shasum dist.tarball (expect shasum e40c391a4f1f909cf2401b68ff88b59ef6e657f6); fresh 'npm install -g tally-agents' into a clean prefix with an empty cache; run tally --version, tally logo (TTY and non-TTY), tally demo, tally doctor in a scratch repo. Report results. No further publishes.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b32-610a-7bc0-b76f-871b4fe2f374","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b32-565c-7863-957f-a5ae63469f4d"},"revision":"retained_01a12b32-610a-7bc0-b76f-873affffdbc6"},"user_input_order":1512},"id":"msg_01a12b32-610a-7bc0-b76f-871b4fe2f374","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791726084.362424,"turn_id":"01a12b32-565c-7863-957f-a5ae63469f4d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] The placeholder was npm's staged processing. Registry now shows tally-agents 0.1.0, latest=0.1.0, shasum e40c391a4f1f909cf2401b68ff88b59ef6e657f6, matching the audited tarball. Redo the fresh install check now (new clean prefix, EMPTY cache so the stage stub is not reused): npm install -g tally-agents, then tally --version, tally logo TTY and non-TTY, tally demo, tally doctor in a scratch repo. Report results.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b34-7b31-7871-aa7e-d5a3cca42db1","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b34-6fe0-7ec1-b268-229ad4a50b38"},"revision":"retained_01a12b34-7b31-7871-aa7e-d5cc87d7f813"},"user_input_order":1516},"id":"msg_01a12b34-7b31-7871-aa7e-d5a3cca42db1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791726222.129211,"turn_id":"01a12b34-6fe0-7ec1-b268-229ad4a50b38"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] New task from Vaibhaav: add 'Entire Trails' to Tally. First investigate and propose, do not build yet. The CLI has 'entire trail' (a trail ties together the context for a branch: create, show, update, list, watch, comment, finding, approve, request-changes, resume, checkout). Read 'entire trail --help' and each subcommand's help, entire agent-help, and docs.entire.io. Try it read-only on a repo where Entire is enabled (fly-doom-jev at /Users/vaibhaav/tally-scratch/fly-doom-jev; chip-design-groundup was enabled today): list existing trails, show one if any exist. Then propose the smallest useful integration, for example: Tally creates one trail per task branch when it starts an attempt, records its routing decision, ceiling, spend, escalation and verify result as trail findings or comments, links the trail on the ledger row and in the PR body and dashboard, and on escalation the next tier resumes with the trail's context. Say what each step needs (auth, repo mirrored on Entire or not, cost, whether it works with both runners and both harnesses) and what you could not verify. No paid runs, no --generate summaries (not approved), no creating trails on his real repos without telling me first; a scratch repo is fine if creation is free. Report the proposal to me in plain terms and wait for my go.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b48-f0a7-7d11-9d53-95c4372c9b5e","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b48-e4b5-73f0-b187-8a6d7ff7b7ef"},"revision":"retained_01a12b48-f0a7-7d11-9d53-95efd868dd54"},"user_input_order":1520},"id":"msg_01a12b48-f0a7-7d11-9d53-95c4372c9b5e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791727562.919568,"turn_id":"01a12b48-e4b5-73f0-b187-8a6d7ff7b7ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Your Trails proposal arrived cut off: I only received the end (from 'whether server creation triggers configured cloud review runners' onward). Write the full proposal to /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/entire-trails-proposal.md (what a trail is, what exists on his repos now, the proposed Tally integration step by step, what each step needs, cost and automation unknowns, what you could not verify, the exact approval you need) and send me a five-line summary with the path.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b4e-1494-7931-87a4-390430f4a032","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b4e-0ce5-7903-9910-42e878418499"},"revision":"retained_01a12b4e-1494-7931-87a4-392db90afac9"},"user_input_order":1525},"id":"msg_01a12b4e-1494-7931-87a4-390430f4a032","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791727899.796484,"turn_id":"01a12b4e-0ce5-7903-9910-42e878418499"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Trails is paused until Vaibhaav decides on the probe; proposal received, thank you. New task from him while you are idle: work out how Tally should use CrustData, and report a proposal before building. What exists: 'tally market' (searches CrustData for companies adopting coding agents, writes .tally/market/latest) and an earlier lead list of 2,085 matches from one unvalidated query, which we agreed is a lead list, not a market size. Judging weights: the agent 30%, use of neatlogs/Entire/cfo.ai 25% (including 'plan a business around the agent'), demo video 20%, building in public 15%, usefulness and originality 10%; CrustData is an additional sponsor. Find out: what the CrustData API offers that is useful here (company search, headcount and hiring signals, tech stack, people search), what our key can access, cost or credit limits per call (do not burn credits: a handful of small read calls at most, and tell me the count); then propose the smallest credible uses, for example (a) validate and tighten the ICP query so the lead count is defensible and can feed the business plan in cfo.ai (share-of-savings pricing, leads not market size), (b) a 'tally market' output good enough to show in the demo video and on the project page, (c) anything that makes the agent itself better rather than only the pitch. Say plainly what is real today, what you could not verify, and what each option costs in time. No code changes yet. Write it to /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/crustdata-proposal.md and send me a five-line summary.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1528},"id":"msg_01a12b5c-dda8-7f83-872c-73cfdf742487","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791728868.776095,"turn_id":"01a12b5c-ced8-7232-8361-429ace3c873c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] CrustData proposal accepted: GO on A+B as one narrow slice (Vaibhaav approved integrating CrustData earlier; this is the careful version of it). Budget: at most 10 CrustData credits in total, small batches, no people or contact lookups, no recurring jobs, no cfo.ai writes. Time-box it: the submission closes 12 Oct 23:55 IST, so aim for a mergeable PR within about four hours and cut scope rather than run long. Order: (1) fix the query (metadata.updated_at) and validate a sample of 10 candidates, labelling each candidate / vendor / hiring intent / verified use / rejected, with source and date; (2) tally market: save provenance (query, retrieved-at, API version, returned vs match count, credits used), a replay-from-saved-query path that makes no API call, a result limit and a maximum-credit estimate before calling; (3) outputs JSON, CSV and a short Markdown report with 5 to 10 reviewed rows, cached so the video can be recorded without calling CrustData; (4) correct the wording everywhere (CLI help, README): 'find and qualify likely pilot companies', never 'companies adopting coding agents', never market size; 2,085 stays only as a historical query count if mentioned at all. Skip option C. Separately, draft (do not write to cfo.ai) a one-page business-plan scenario for a cfo.ai page: share-of-savings pricing, leads -\u003e assumed conversion -\u003e pilots -\u003e revenue, every assumption labelled as an assumption, savings based on Tally's measured costs not headcount; put it in /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/cfoai-business-plan-draft.md for Vaibhaav to approve before anything is written to cfo.ai. Tell me when the PR is open.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b66-0640-7dc3-9552-d6e10e9fb0cd","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b65-fcc9-7de2-bb12-3870ce9698b0"},"revision":"retained_01a12b66-0640-7dc3-9552-d70612932b6a"},"user_input_order":1535},"id":"msg_01a12b66-0640-7dc3-9552-d6e10e9fb0cd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791729468.99201,"turn_id":"01a12b65-fcc9-7de2-bb12-3870ce9698b0"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] To save you time: I have written the cfo.ai business-plan draft myself (/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-business-plan-draft.md), so drop that part of your task. Its funnel table needs one thing from you: the number of qualified leads from your reviewed sample, with the labels. Vaibhaav is asking for CrustData to move fast: open the PR as soon as the fixed query, the 10-row reviewed sample, provenance, the no-API replay and the corrected wording are in; send me the reviewed sample's path and counts the moment it exists, even before the PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b74-5c5c-74e3-91d9-6ffbff9627db","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b74-5aee-7e40-9f78-c625e16c6d30"},"revision":"retained_01a12b74-5c5c-74e3-91d9-701e507016e5"},"user_input_order":1545},"id":"msg_01a12b74-5c5c-74e3-91d9-6ffbff9627db","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791730408.540321,"turn_id":"01a12b74-5aee-7e40-9f78-c625e16c6d30"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] I read market-reviewed/report.md. The mechanics are right (provenance, labels, replay, honest wording). The sample itself is weak for judges: 56,477 matches, 10 rows that are all firmographic fits with zero coding-tool evidence, at 0.63 credits a row. Before you open the PR, add the second stage your own proposal recommended, because it is the only route to real signal: Job Search (0.03 credits/result) for engineering job posts whose content.description names coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Codex, 'AI coding agent'), 20 to 30 results, labelled 'hiring intent' with company, title, source URL and date, deduplicated by company; drop ambiguous matches. Then the report leads with those rows and keeps the firmographic sample as a secondary table. I am raising your CrustData cap to 20 credits in total for this (you have used 6.3); avoid the premium company filters that made the first query 0.63 a row. If Job Search returns nothing usable, say so plainly and ship the PR with what you have. Also: all three repos are now mirrored to Entire and show 'ready' (fly-doom-jev, chip-design-groundup, neatlogs-hack); checkpoint search now reaches them, but 'entire trail list --repo gh/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/fly-doom-jev' returns 'trail API: repository not found (404)'. After the CrustData PR, pick Trails back up: find out why (propagation, trails not enabled for the account, or a different repo reference), read-only first, then the one-trail probe on fly-doom-jev that Vaibhaav has approved, stopping if anything asks for payment.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12b74-a87a-79c0-a318-fef44fcd7c42","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12b74-a73f-7921-9d75-8f8e5f93a685"},"revision":"retained_01a12b74-a87a-79c0-a318-ff13758445e7"},"user_input_order":1547},"id":"msg_01a12b74-a87a-79c0-a318-fef44fcd7c42","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791730428.026238,"turn_id":"01a12b74-a73f-7921-9d75-8f8e5f93a685"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #118 gated with #119 (679 tests x2, typecheck, build, dry runs) and merged; main is 61899ce. The job-intent report is exactly what was needed, thank you. Vaibhaav has decided: Entire Trails is DROPPED from the submission; do no more work on it (your probe write-up stays as the record). No npm packaging yet either; he will say when. Stand by.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12c09-826b-74b3-8d79-8a3ba2df8e54","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12c09-48f4-7ee1-9b80-626459990dbd"},"revision":"retained_01a12c09-826b-74b3-8d79-8a5be6adae23"},"user_input_order":1556},"id":"msg_01a12c09-826b-74b3-8d79-8a3ba2df8e54","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791740183.147838,"turn_id":"01a12c09-48f4-7ee1-9b80-626459990dbd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"https://tally-agents-pi.vercel.app/\nadd this video in the website in the placeholder\n\nAttached files (read these files in the workspace):\n- .ao/attachments/attachment-fb0de3b60183864ef29276a21a5ef37a.m4v","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1558},"id":"msg_01a12c71-ad9a-7b22-bb3b-a5745a54e207","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791747009.946267,"turn_id":"01a12c71-aa70-7aa3-8082-f9265ce5d816"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"merge and update the deplyment","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12c76-944a-7f12-aff8-9636cc715b0f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12c76-936c-75c1-8580-bcbcd6febdd3"},"revision":"retained_01a12c76-944a-7f12-aff8-965ebe9eac1a"},"user_input_order":1564},"id":"msg_01a12c76-944a-7f12-aff8-9636cc715b0f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791747331.146135,"turn_id":"01a12c76-936c-75c1-8580-bcbcd6febdd3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Context: a hackathon mentor reviewed Tally and said, in short: use neatlogs traces to DRIVE decisions, not just log them (read past cost and tokens per task type from the traces to pick the model and set the cap; when a capped attempt fails, look at the trace to see why, e.g. ran out of budget or a tool failed, and escalate based on that); show a before and after (routing v1 vs v2, cost per task and success rate from the traces: 'judges want exactly that'); test whether Entire graph size predicts real cost across the completed tasks and chart it, mixing in simpler signals (issue length, files mentioned) if it does not; and record one run where the cap kicks in and it escalates ('your best moment'). Vaibhaav wants this done today; submission closes 12 Oct 23:55 IST, so work must be merged and evidenced by about 20:00 IST. main is 7509d37 and other people (adot-7, TheEleventhAvatar) are also pushing to it: rebase often, keep PRs small, tell me the PR number and I gate and merge. Say plainly what is not done or not proven.\n\nYOUR PART (lane B, the CFO agent's decisions and the analysis; this is your original lane). (1) Find out and tell me first, in three lines: on the latest real runs (e.g. run-20261011-190131Z, /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof/.tally/runs/run-20261011-190131Z) did routing use real history read from neatlogs traces, or the built-in priors? Early runs said 'No usable history exists ... so it uses the prior'. (2) Make the traces drive the decision, small PRs: (a) ceilings: today they are fixed per size and tier in tally.yaml; set each attempt's ceiling from observed cost for that size and tier in the trace history when enough observations exist (for example a high percentile times a margin), never above the configured ceiling, falling back to config otherwise; (b) the decision text and the decision trace must state exactly what history was used (n observations, pass rate, typical cost, source neatlogs or local) or that the prior was used; (c) escalation: when an attempt fails or is stopped, read that attempt's neatlogs worker trace and classify why (hit the ceiling mid-work, a tool or command failed, tests failed, permission refused, model unavailable), record the classification and its evidence on the ledger row, and let it choose the next step (same tier retry is not allowed; escalate, or stop without escalating when a stronger model would hit the same wall). If the trace cannot be read, fall back to today's ledger-based reason and say so. Tests with fakes for each class. (3) The analysis, as a command or script that reads real data only (ledgers and neatlogs traces from all real runs so far, plus lane A's baseline-comparison results when they arrive): cost per task and success rate, before (prior-only routing, and everything-on-top-tier baseline) against after (trace-driven routing); and the mentor's size test: Entire graph size, files touched, issue length and files named, each against real cost, with the correlation stated honestly including 'no signal' if that is the result (most of our tasks were small docs changes, so say what the data can and cannot show). Output a short Markdown report with two or three simple charts as SVG or PNG to /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/ so lane C can put them on the site and he can show them in the video. No invented numbers. Lane A owns the paid runs and engine/real.ts; coordinate through me if you need a hook there.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1568},"id":"msg_01a12f5b-217a-79e1-af81-801455de7224","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791795863.930638,"turn_id":"01a12f5b-1663-7372-806d-f48a963c13b7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] STEER from orchestrator, reply 'ack' first: APPROVED: add the optional LedgerRow.failureAssessment field (schema, types, tests) AND do the engine/real.ts wiring yourself in PR #140 (diagnose the ended row, persist it, pass it and history into decideEscalation). #140 currently conflicts with main 5ede9e0 in agent/escalation.ts: rebase, resolve, push, tell me the head. Lane A's signals for the five comparison tasks: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json and mentor-comparison-preparation.md.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"user_input_order":1576},"id":"msg_01a12f81-08bc-7600-be75-f929353e7c68","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791798347.964533,"turn_id":"01a12f5b-1663-7372-806d-f48a963c13b7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Audit received, clear. To avoid waiting on lane A (it is on paid runs and is not editing engine/real.ts today): you may add the hooks in engine/real.ts yourself for this work: pass history to escalation, pass the previous attempt's workerTraceId, a diagnostic trace-read port, and persisting the failure classification and evidence on the ledger row (schema fields too). Keep those edits minimal and in their own small PR so a conflict with others' pushes is easy to resolve. Provenance and observed caps first, as you planned.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12f92-969a-7ce0-9d5a-bc2f89d9a634","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12f92-95da-7b42-89ee-1f9a1fccbac4"},"revision":"retained_01a12f92-969a-7ce0-9d5a-bc42ab741aed"},"user_input_order":1590},"id":"msg_01a12f92-969a-7ce0-9d5a-bc2f89d9a634","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791799498.394349,"turn_id":"01a12f92-95da-7b42-89ee-1f9a1fccbac4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #138 gated (tests x2, typecheck, build, dry runs) and merged; main is 5a5b5a9. Carry on with the failure-diagnosis slice; you already have my go to add the engine/real.ts hook yourself. Your finding that the stopped FDJ-3 trace exposes no outputs or errors matters: classify from the trace only what the trace can actually show, fall back to the ledger reason otherwise, and label which source each classification came from. Do not present a ledger-based reason as trace-derived.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12f92-c0c0-75e1-89cf-fec99abc52a4","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12f92-c00f-73d2-bd4b-daae5dbbf4ba"},"revision":"retained_01a12f92-c0c0-75e1-89cf-fee881c53743"},"user_input_order":1592},"id":"msg_01a12f92-c0c0-75e1-89cf-fec99abc52a4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791799509.184871,"turn_id":"01a12f92-c00f-73d2-bd4b-daae5dbbf4ba"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] Yes to all of it: add LedgerRow.failureAssessment exactly as you describe (schema, types, tests). And do the engine wiring YOURSELF, do not wait for lane A: it is busy with a stuck escalation and the baseline runs. You have my explicit go to edit engine/real.ts for this: call diagnoseAttempt on the ended row, persist the assessment, pass it and ports.history into escalation. Keep it one small PR.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12f92-e3a4-7da1-b511-24229882488d","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12f92-e2fb-7e13-bf52-c1a5c6c5f2c3"},"revision":"retained_01a12f92-e3a4-7da1-b511-2441045a9e5c"},"user_input_order":1594},"id":"msg_01a12f92-e3a4-7da1-b511-24229882488d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791799518.116875,"turn_id":"01a12f92-e2fb-7e13-bf52-c1a5c6c5f2c3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] APPROVED, sent twice already, in case it has not reached you: (1) add the optional LedgerRow.failureAssessment field with schema, types and tests; (2) do the engine/real.ts wiring YOURSELF: diagnose the ended row, persist row.failureAssessment, pass it and the #138 history into decideEscalation. Do not wait for lane A; it is fixing a completion-state bug in the same file (workers ending in needs_input with finished work), so keep your real.ts diff to those few lines, rebase on main 5ede9e0, and expect to rebase once more when its PR lands. Open the PR as soon as it is green and tell me. Then the real-data analysis.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12f93-001e-76d0-8249-a5161ad8c700","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a"},"revision":"retained_01a12f93-001e-76d0-8249-a534ac619973"},"user_input_order":1596},"id":"msg_01a12f93-001e-76d0-8249-a5161ad8c700","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791799525.406521,"turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #140 (d49c990) gated together with lane A's #141 and merged; main is 0ab7950 (783 tests). Next: (1) the analysis script PR; (2) key history by actual model, not only tier name, so learned caps do not pool Codex and Claude costs; (3) be ready to regenerate the routing-evidence report when lane A's cap retry and baseline comparison land: I will send you the paths.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12f93-5cec-78f2-b2ca-dcb9e3977f52","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a"},"revision":"retained_01a12f93-5cec-78f2-b2ca-dcd2fdfa198d"},"user_input_order":1598},"id":"msg_01a12f93-5cec-78f2-b2ca-dcb9e3977f52","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791799549.164692,"turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"There are merge conflicts on PR #140 \"Classify worker trace failures before escalation\" (ao/neatlogs-hack-5/trace-failure-diagnosis → main). Rebase onto the base branch and resolve them.\nPR: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/140","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"},{"first_turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a","server_name":"ao","tool_name":"html_preview"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12fa1-4bd4-79a0-9df0-4a33cc22e42e","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12fa1-4aee-75e1-80bf-2d19b3e7cb62"},"revision":"retained_01a12fa1-4bd5-7753-bffa-23c7fce3194f"},"user_input_order":1606},"id":"msg_01a12fa1-4bd4-79a0-9df0-4a33cc22e42e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791800462.292976,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-4aee-75e1-80bf-2d19b3e7cb62"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] From lane A for your analysis: sizing signals for the five baseline-comparison tasks (graph and text signals at plan time) are at /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json, with the task table and caveats in mentor-comparison-preparation.md in the same folder. Sizes small/small/medium/medium/large; files 1/2/4/3/3; dependents unmeasured/26/70/35/91. Costs for these five will come when the paid comparison runs (it is waiting on lane A's completion-state fix). Build the report so it fills in from that folder when the results land.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"},{"first_turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a","server_name":"ao","tool_name":"html_preview"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12fa1-8a7f-7bf0-b2aa-9d49bc51653a","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"revision":"retained_01a12fa1-8a80-7330-9d6f-6fc83e62a6ba"},"user_input_order":1608},"id":"msg_01a12fa1-8a7f-7bf0-b2aa-9d49bc51653a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791800478.335941,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] #144 gated together with adot-7's #137 and merged; main is 9f18111. Real data for your report: the cap-and-escalate run is at /private/tmp/tally-cap-retry.Apm5J4/.tally/runs/run-20261012-100856Z (attempt 1 cheap stopped at ceiling, failureAssessment ceiling/ledger; attempt 2 middle passed; fly-doom-jev PR #17). Lane A will run the comparison as three passes on the same tasks: A top-tier baseline, B Tally routing v1 (priors), C Tally routing v2 (trace history from pass B). Make the report present exactly those three cohorts side by side (cost per task, pass rate, attempts) plus the size-against-cost chart using the five tasks' graph signals, and regenerate as each pass lands; I will send paths. Keep every caveat.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751","server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js"},{"first_turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a","server_name":"ao","tool_name":"html_preview"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12fa4-048c-7270-980b-169f5307242f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"revision":"retained_01a12fa4-048c-7270-980b-16b12493bc53"},"user_input_order":1610},"id":"msg_01a12fa4-048c-7270-980b-169f5307242f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791800640.652929,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb5937fc487d08fab7c7b98c1dda6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_0546e4cf5cd147e492a4d4fa96f69279","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb594015087d0b767b730be743a88","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/comparison-evidence.ts\\n@@\\n export interface ComparisonOutcome {\\n@@\\n   skipped: boolean;\\n+  attempts: number;\\n@@\\n-export interface ComparisonRun { run: RunState; ledger: LedgerRow[]; path: string }\\n+export type ComparisonPass = 'A' | 'B' | 'C';\\n+export interface ComparisonRun { run: RunState; ledger: LedgerRow[]; path: string; pass?: ComparisonPass }\\n@@\\n-  const rows = measurements.map(item =\u003e ({ ...item, baseline: [] as ComparisonOutcome[], tally: [] as ComparisonOutcome[] }));\\n+  const rows = measurements.map(item =\u003e ({ ...item, A: [] as ComparisonOutcome[], B: [] as ComparisonOutcome[], C: [] as ComparisonOutcome[] }));\\n@@\\n-  for (const { run, ledger, path } of runs) {\\n+  for (const { run, ledger, path, pass } of runs) {\\n@@\\n-      const reason = run.baseCommit !== plan.baseCommit ? 'base SHA differs or is missing'\\n+      const reason = !pass ? 'comparison pass not explicitly labelled A/B/C'\\n+        : (pass === 'A') !== (run.mode === 'baseline') ? 'run mode differs from labelled comparison pass'\\n+        : run.baseCommit !== plan.baseCommit ? 'base SHA differs or is missing'\\n@@\\n-      row[run.mode].push({ runId: run.runId, mode: run.mode, repeat: run.repeat ?? null,\\n-        costNanos: outcome.costNanos, passed: outcome.passed, errored: outcome.errored, skipped: outcome.skipped, source: path });\\n+      row[pass!].push({ runId: run.runId, mode: run.mode, repeat: run.repeat ?? null,\\n+        costNanos: outcome.costNanos, passed: outcome.passed, errored: outcome.errored, skipped: outcome.skipped, attempts: outcome.attempts, source: path });\\n       observations.push({ ...outcome, size: row.size, filesTouched: row.filesTouched, graphNodes: row.graphNodes,\\n-        issueLength: row.issueLength, filesNamed: row.filesNamed, textSource: 'plan-query', signalSource: 'comparison-plan' });\\n+        issueLength: row.issueLength, filesNamed: row.filesNamed, textSource: 'plan-query', signalSource: 'comparison-plan', comparisonPass: pass });\\n@@\\n-  return { baseCommit: plan.baseCommit, measuredAt: typeof plan.measuredAt === 'string' ? plan.measuredAt : null, rows, observations, excluded };\\n+  const summaries = (['A', 'B', 'C'] as const).map(pass =\u003e {\\n+    const outcomes = rows.flatMap(row =\u003e row[pass]);\\n+    return { pass, outcomes: outcomes.length, coveredTasks: rows.filter(row =\u003e row[pass].length).length, plannedTasks: rows.length,\\n+      attempts: outcomes.reduce((sum, row) =\u003e sum + row.attempts, 0), passed: outcomes.filter(row =\u003e row.passed).length,\\n+      meanCostUsd: outcomes.length ? outcomes.reduce((sum, row) =\u003e sum + row.costNanos, 0) / outcomes.length / 1e9 : null,\\n+      successRate: outcomes.length ? outcomes.filter(row =\u003e row.passed).length / outcomes.length : null };\\n+  });\\n+  return { baseCommit: plan.baseCommit, measuredAt: typeof plan.measuredAt === 'string' ? plan.measuredAt : null, rows, observations, summaries, excluded };\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/evidence.ts\\n@@\\n   signalSource?: 'comparison-plan';\\n+  comparisonPass?: 'A' | 'B' | 'C';\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts\\n@@\\n-const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, tasks: [run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run' };\\n+const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, mode: 'tally' as const, tasks: [run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run', pass: 'B' as const };\\n@@\\n-    expect(result.rows[0]).toMatchObject({ size: 'small', filesTouched: 2, dependents: 26, graphNodes: 12, baseline: [], tally: [] });\\n+    expect(result.rows[0]).toMatchObject({ size: 'small', filesTouched: 2, dependents: 26, graphNodes: 12, A: [], B: [], C: [] });\\n@@\\n-      ...input, run: { ...input.run, runId: 'baseline-run', mode: 'baseline', repeat: 1 },\\n+      ...input, pass: 'A', run: { ...input.run, runId: 'baseline-run', mode: 'baseline', repeat: 1 },\\n@@\\n-    expect(result.rows[0]?.tally[0]?.costNanos).toBe(ledger[0]!.estimatedCostNanos);\\n-    expect(result.rows[0]?.baseline[0]).toMatchObject({ costNanos: 123, passed: true, repeat: 1 });\\n+    expect(result.rows[0]?.B[0]?.costNanos).toBe(ledger[0]!.estimatedCostNanos);\\n+    expect(result.rows[0]?.A[0]).toMatchObject({ costNanos: 123, passed: true, repeat: 1 });\\n@@\\n-    for (const baseCommit of [undefined, 'b'.repeat(40)]) {\\n+    for (const baseCommit of [null, 'b'.repeat(40)]) {\\n@@\\n-    expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [skipped]).rows[0]?.tally[0]).toMatchObject({ costNanos: 0, passed: false, skipped: true });\\n+    expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [skipped]).rows[0]?.B[0]).toMatchObject({ costNanos: 0, passed: false, skipped: true });\\n   });\\n+\\n+  it('does not infer B/C from routing text and keeps C explicitly separate from B', () =\u003e {\\n+    expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [{ ...input, pass: undefined }]).observations).toEqual([]);\\n+    const result = comparisonEvidence(plan, [input, { ...input, pass: 'C', run: { ...input.run, runId: 'v2-run' }, ledger: [{ ...ledger[0]!, runId: 'v2-run' }] }]);\\n+    expect(result.rows[0]?.B).toHaveLength(1);\\n+    expect(result.rows[0]?.C).toHaveLength(1);\\n+    expect(result.summaries.find(summary =\u003e summary.pass === 'A')).toMatchObject({ meanCostUsd: null, successRate: null });\\n+    expect(result.observations[1]?.comparisonPass).toBe('C');\\n+  });\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800724.1884873,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_0546e4cf5cd147e492a4d4fa96f69279","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fa5-d4e4-71a3-aefe-6b5706572e8d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800759.524874,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb5cf471887d0a20423ae43aadb76","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_40c7d4d22320427e9dbfdd8e299ee8af","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb5cf8c2487d0b2e501062350c1fa","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/scripts/routing-evidence.mjs\\n@@\\n import { taskEvidence, cohortSummary, correlate } from '../dist/agent/evidence.js';\\n+import { comparisonEvidence } from '../dist/agent/comparison-evidence.js';\\n@@\\n-if (args.includes('--help') || !option('--manifest') || !option('--out')) {\\n-  console.log('Usage: npm run build, then node scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest runs.json --out \u003cdirectory\u003e [--issues issues.json] [--live-traces]');\\n+if (args.includes('--help') || (!option('--manifest') \u0026\u0026 !option('--comparison-dir')) || !option('--out')) {\\n+  console.log('Usage: npm run build, then node scripts/routing-evidence.mjs [--manifest runs.json] [--comparison-dir \u003cfolder\u003e] --out \u003cdirectory\u003e [--issues issues.json] [--live-traces]');\\n@@\\n-const manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(resolve(option('--manifest')), 'utf8'));\\n+const manifest = option('--manifest') ? JSON.parse(await readFile(resolve(option('--manifest')), 'utf8')) : [];\\n if (!Array.isArray(manifest) || manifest.some(value =\u003e typeof value !== 'string')) throw new Error('Manifest must be an array of audited run-directory paths.');\\n+const comparisonDir = option('--comparison-dir') ? resolve(option('--comparison-dir')) : null;\\n+let plan = null;\\n+const passAssignments = new Map();\\n+if (comparisonDir) {\\n+  plan = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(comparisonDir, 'mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json'), 'utf8'));\\n+  let passes = {};\\n+  try { passes = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(comparisonDir, 'comparison-passes.json'), 'utf8')); }\\n+  catch (error) { if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error; }\\n+  if (!passes || typeof passes !== 'object' || Array.isArray(passes)) throw new Error('comparison-passes.json must be an A/B/C object');\\n+  for (const [pass, paths] of Object.entries(passes)) {\\n+    if (!['A', 'B', 'C'].includes(pass) || !Array.isArray(paths) || paths.some(path =\u003e typeof path !== 'string')) throw new Error('Comparison pass must be A/B/C with an array of run paths');\\n+    for (const path of paths) {\\n+      const absolute = resolve(comparisonDir, path);\\n+      if (passAssignments.has(absolute) \u0026\u0026 passAssignments.get(absolute) !== pass) throw new Error('One run path cannot belong to two comparison passes');\\n+      passAssignments.set(absolute, pass); manifest.push(absolute);\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+}\\n@@\\n-const seen = new Set(), tasks = [], attempts = [], exclusions = [], sources = [];\\n+const seen = new Set(), tasks = [], attempts = [], exclusions = [], sources = [], closedRuns = [];\\n for (const entry of manifest) {\\n-  const path = await realpath(entry);\\n-  const run = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(path, 'run.json'), 'utf8'));\\n-  const ledger = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(path, 'ledger.json'), 'utf8'));\\n+  let path, run, ledger;\\n+  try {\\n+    path = await realpath(entry);\\n+    run = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(path, 'run.json'), 'utf8'));\\n+    ledger = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(path, 'ledger.json'), 'utf8'));\\n+  } catch (error) {\\n+    if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\\n+    exclusions.push({ path: entry, reason: 'run files not available yet' }); continue;\\n+  }\\n@@\\n   seen.add(run.runId);\\n+  const pass = passAssignments.get(resolve(entry));\\n+  closedRuns.push({ run, ledger, path, pass });\\n@@\\n }\\n+const comparison = plan ? comparisonEvidence(plan, closedRuns) : null;\\n+if (comparison) {\\n+  for (const observation of comparison.observations) {\\n+    const index = tasks.findIndex(task =\u003e task.runId === observation.runId \u0026\u0026 task.taskId === observation.taskId);\\n+    if (index \u003e= 0) tasks[index] = observation;\\n+  }\\n+}\\n@@\\n-const eligible = tasks.filter(task =\u003e task.passed \u0026\u0026 !task.errored);\\n+const eligible = (comparison ? comparison.observations : tasks).filter(task =\u003e task.passed \u0026\u0026 !task.errored);\\n@@\\n ].map(([key, label]) =\u003e ({ key, label, ...correlate(eligible.map(task =\u003e [task[key], task.costNanos / 1e9])) }));\\n+const signalsByPass = comparison ? ['A', 'B', 'C'].flatMap(pass =\u003e signals.map(signal =\u003e ({ pass, key: signal.key, label: signal.label,\\n+  ...correlate(eligible.filter(task =\u003e task.comparisonPass === pass).map(task =\u003e [task[signal.key], task.costNanos / 1e9])) }))) : [];\\n@@\\n-const reportData = { generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(), sources, exclusions, cohorts, signals, tasks,\\n+const reportData = { generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(), sources, exclusions, cohorts, signals, signalsByPass, comparison, tasks,\\n@@\\n-const keys = ['runId', 'repo', 'taskId', 'cohort', 'costNanos', 'passed', 'errored', 'skipped', 'attempts', 'size', 'graphNodes', 'filesTouched', 'issueLength', 'filesNamed', 'textSource', 'models', 'source'];\\n+const keys = ['runId', 'repo', 'taskId', 'cohort', 'comparisonPass', 'costNanos', 'passed', 'errored', 'skipped', 'attempts', 'size', 'graphNodes', 'filesTouched', 'issueLength', 'filesNamed', 'textSource', 'signalSource', 'models', 'source'];\\n@@\\n async function barChart(file, title, key, format) {\\n-  const max = Math.max(...cohorts.map(row =\u003e row[key] ?? 0), 0.01);\\n-  const body = cohorts.map((row, i) =\u003e {\\n+  const chartRows = comparison ? comparison.summaries.map(row =\u003e ({ ...row, cohort: { A: 'A: top baseline', B: 'B: Tally v1', C: 'C: Tally v2' }[row.pass], tasks: row.outcomes })) : cohorts;\\n+  const max = Math.max(...chartRows.map(row =\u003e row[key] ?? 0), 0.01);\\n+  const body = chartRows.map((row, i) =\u003e {\\n@@\\n-  const points = rows.map(row =\u003e `\u003ccircle cx=\\\"${x0 + row[signal.key] / maxX * 330}\\\" cy=\\\"${y0 + 180 - row.costNanos / 1e9 / maxY * 165}\\\" r=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"#187d5b\\\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003e${escape(`${row.runId}/${row.taskId}, $${(row.costNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)}`)}\u003c/title\u003e\u003c/circle\u003e`).join('');\\n+  const points = rows.map(row =\u003e `\u003ccircle cx=\\\"${x0 + row[signal.key] / maxX * 330}\\\" cy=\\\"${y0 + 180 - row.costNanos / 1e9 / maxY * 165}\\\" r=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"${{ A: '#356bbb', B: '#ae4739', C: '#187d5b' }[row.comparisonPass] ?? '#187d5b'}\\\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003e${escape(`${row.comparisonPass ?? ''} ${row.runId}/${row.taskId}, $${(row.costNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)}`)}\u003c/title\u003e\u003c/circle\u003e`).join('');\\n@@\\n-await writeFile(join(out, 'size-cost.svg'), svg('Sizing signals versus completed-task estimated cost', 650, scatter + '\u003ctext x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"625\\\"\u003eSuccessful task executions only; small, selected sample. Text may be reconstructed from current issue bodies.\u003c/text\u003e'));\\n+await writeFile(join(out, 'size-cost.svg'), svg('Sizing signals versus completed-task estimated cost', 650, scatter + `\u003ctext x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"625\\\"\u003e${comparison ? 'A blue: baseline; B red: v1; C green: v2. Matched plan signals; repeats are not independent samples.' : 'Successful task executions only; small, selected sample. Text may be reconstructed from current issue bodies.'}\u003c/text\u003e`));\\n@@\\n const fmt = value =\u003e value === null ? 'not measured' : value.toFixed(3);\\n+const outcomeCell = outcomes =\u003e outcomes.length ? outcomes.map(row =\u003e `$${(row.costNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)} / ${row.passed ? 'passed' : row.skipped ? 'skipped' : row.errored ? 'error' : 'failed'} / ${row.attempts} attempts (${row.runId})`).join('\u003cbr\u003e') : 'pending';\\n+const comparisonLines = comparison ? [\\n+  '## Three-Pass Comparison', '', `Plan measured ${comparison.measuredAt ?? 'date unavailable'}, pinned base ${comparison.baseCommit}. Signals source: ${comparisonDir}/mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json.`, '',\\n+  '| Pass | Covered tasks | Task outcomes | Mean cost/task USD | Pass rate | Attempts |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|',\\n+  ...comparison.summaries.map(row =\u003e `| ${row.pass}: ${{ A: 'top-tier baseline', B: 'Tally v1 (priors)', C: 'Tally v2 (trace history)' }[row.pass]} | ${row.coveredTasks}/${row.plannedTasks} | ${row.outcomes} | ${row.meanCostUsd === null ? 'pending' : row.meanCostUsd.toFixed(5)} | ${row.successRate === null ? 'pending' : (row.successRate * 100).toFixed(1) + '%'} | ${row.outcomes ? row.attempts : 'pending'} |`), '',\\n+  '| Task | Size | Targets | Dependents | Graph nodes | Text chars | Named paths | A: cost/verdict/attempts | B: cost/verdict/attempts | C: cost/verdict/attempts |',\\n+  '|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|',\\n+  ...comparison.rows.map(row =\u003e `| ${row.taskId} | ${row.size} | ${row.filesTouched} | ${row.dependents ?? 'unmeasured'} | ${row.graphNodes ?? 'unmeasured'} | ${row.issueLength} | ${row.filesNamed} | ${outcomeCell(row.A)} | ${outcomeCell(row.B)} | ${outcomeCell(row.C)} |`), '',\\n+  'Pass labels are explicit experiment assignments, not proof that history affected every route in C. Actual routing provenance remains in tasks.csv. Costs only come from matching real ledgers; plan signals never supply spend. Missing passes/tasks stay pending; partial coverage is not a completed comparison. No savings claim before all three passes cover the same tasks. A single repeat establishes no statistical spread.', '',\\n+  `Comparison join exclusions: ${comparison.excluded.length} (base/text/pass-label mismatches retained in results.json).`, '',\\n+] : [];\\n+const capLines = closedRuns.flatMap(({ run, ledger }) =\u003e ledger.filter(row =\u003e row.result === 'stopped').map(row =\u003e {\\n+  const next = ledger.find(candidate =\u003e candidate.escalatedFrom === row.attemptId \u0026\u0026 !candidate.attemptId.endsWith(':handoff'));\\n+  return `| ${run.runId} / ${row.taskId} | ${row.tier}: $${(row.estimatedCostNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)} / cap $${(row.ceilingNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)} | ${row.failureAssessment ? `${row.failureAssessment.kind} / ${row.failureAssessment.source}` : 'classification not recorded'} | ${next ? `${next.tier}: ${next.result} / $${(next.estimatedCostNanos / 1e9).toFixed(5)}` : 'no escalation row'} | ${row.checkpointId ?? 'none'} | ${row.workerTraceId ?? 'unverified'} |`;\\n+}));\\n const lines = [\\n   '# Routing evidence', '', `Generated ${reportData.generatedAt}. ${sources.length} closed real runs; ${tasks.length} task outcomes (including skipped).`, '',\\n+  ...comparisonLines,\\n@@\\n   ...signals.map(signal =\u003e `| ${signal.label} | ${signal.n} | ${fmt(signal.pearson)} | ${fmt(signal.spearman)} | ${signal.interpretation} |`), '',\\n+  ...(comparison ? ['| Pass | Signal | Successful pairs | Pearson r | Spearman rho |', '|---|---|---:|---:|---:|',\\n+    ...signalsByPass.map(signal =\u003e `| ${signal.pass} | ${signal.label} | ${signal.n} | ${fmt(signal.pearson)} | ${fmt(signal.spearman)} |`), '',\\n+    'The size chart uses only comparison outcomes at the pinned base with measured plan signals, not unrelated historical tasks. Pooled correlations mix model prices; per-pass coefficients are also reported. Repeated tasks across passes are not independent observations. New target files and named context can make graph targets differ from literal file mentions.', ''] : []),\\n@@\\n   'Costs here are normalized list-price/AO estimates from the real ledger, not invoices. History trace names repeat those recorded estimates. Public worker traces can report zero cost/tokens when hooks export tool activity only; that does not mean the worker was free.', '',\\n+  '## Cap and Escalation Evidence', '',\\n+  '| Run/task | Stopped spend and cap | Failure class/source | Next attempt | Stopped checkpoint | Worker trace id |',\\n+  '|---|---|---|---|---|---|', ...capLines, '',\\n+  'Metering/polling lag can overshoot a cap. A stored worker trace id is not fresh read-back verification; see the readback section. Ledger-derived ceiling classifications remain ledger-derived even after trace delivery recovers.', '',\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npm run typecheck\",max_output_tokens:1500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npx vitest run agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800783.6343071,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_40c7d4d22320427e9dbfdd8e299ee8af","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fa7-622f-7541-b6ed-e6a966441b2e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800861.231099,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"87b641\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.203852792,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":17,\"output\":\"\\n\u003e tally-agents@0.1.0 typecheck\\n\u003e tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ab915f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.38327725,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":774,\"output\":\"\\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5\\n\\n ❯ agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts (7 tests | 3 failed) 44ms\\n   ❯ comparison plan evidence (7)\\n     × joins actual costs and verdicts by base and task, without using proposed cost 2ms\\n     × excludes dry/active runs and duplicates and retains skipped real tasks 1ms\\n     × does not infer B/C from routing text and keeps C explicitly separate from B 0ms\\n\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 3 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\\n\\n FAIL  agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts \u003e comparison plan evidence \u003e joins actual costs and verdicts by base and task, without using proposed cost\\nAssertionError: expected undefined to be 130000000 // Object.is equality\\n\\n- Expected:\\n130000000\\n\\n+ Received:\\nundefined\\n\\n ❯ agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts:27:45\\n     25|       ledger: [{ ...ledger[0]!, runId: 'baseline-run', estimatedCostNa…\\n     26|     }]);\\n     27|     expect(result.rows[0]?.B[0]?.costNanos).toBe(ledger[0]!.estimatedC…\\n       |                                             ^\\n     28|     expect(result.rows[0]?.A[0]).toMatchObject({ costNanos: 123, passe…\\n     29|     expect(result.observations[0]).toMatchObject({ issueLength: 100, g…\\n\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/3]⎯\\n\\n FAIL  agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts \u003e comparison plan evidence \u003e excludes dry/active runs and duplicates and retains skipped real tasks\\nAssertionError: expected [] to have a length of 1 but got +0\\n\\n- Expected\\n+ Received\\n\\n- 1\\n+ 0\\n\\n ❯ agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts:43:67\\n     41|   it('excludes dry/active runs and duplicates and retains skipped real…\\n     42|     expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [{ ...input, run: { ...input.run, …\\n     43|     expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [input, input]).observations).toHa…\\n       |                                                                   ^\\n     44|     const skipped = { ...input, ledger: [], run: { ...input.run, tasks…\\n     45|     expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [skipped]).rows[0]?.B[0]).toMatchO…\\n\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[2/3]⎯\\n\\n FAIL  agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts \u003e comparison plan evidence \u003e does not infer B/C from routing text and keeps C explicitly separate from B\\nAssertionError: expected [] to have a length of 1 but got +0\\n\\n- Expected\\n+ Received\\n\\n- 1\\n+ 0\\n\\n ❯ agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts:51:31\\n     49|     expect(comparisonEvidence(plan, [{ ...input, pass: undefined }]).o…\\n     50|     const result = comparisonEvidence(plan, [input, { ...input, pass: …\\n     51|     expect(result.rows[0]?.B).toHaveLength(1);\\n       |                               ^\\n     52|     expect(result.rows[0]?.C).toHaveLength(1);\\n     53|     expect(result.summaries.find(summary =\u003e summary.pass === 'A')).toM…\\n\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[3/3]⎯\\n\\n\\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\\n      Tests  3 failed | 4 passed (7)\\n   Start at  15:57:41\\n   Duration  136ms (tests 62%, transform 25%, setup 7%, import 4%, worker 2%)\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6228ab487d0957bd1667a6cd4a7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_44bca359caf84acf90b23f91732ed011","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb622b5f887d0bcec198d35d68129","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts\\n@@\\n-const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, mode: 'tally' as const, tasks: [run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run', pass: 'B' as const };\\n+const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, mode: 'tally' as const, tasks: [{ ...run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!, impact: undefined }] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run', pass: 'B' as const };\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npm run build\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npx vitest run agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts\",max_output_tokens:1400}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"node scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/input-runs.json --comparison-dir /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2 --issues /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/issues-current.json --out /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Generate the requested A/B/C report with plan signals and explicit pending costs, using cached readback only.\",max_output_tokens:1600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800866.7142413,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_44bca359caf84acf90b23f91732ed011","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fa7-aea4-79f3-89e9-bf8cdfd7e42b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800880.804433,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1ef649\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.191191959,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":15,\"output\":\"\\n\u003e tally-agents@0.1.0 build\\n\u003e tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"708e80\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.334685459,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":59,\"output\":\"\\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5\\n\\n\\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\\n   Start at  15:57:56\\n   Duration  110ms (tests 57%, transform 28%, setup 8%, import 4%, worker 3%)\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"882f8a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":575,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence\\\",\\n  \\\"runs\\\": 20,\\n  \\\"tasks\\\": 25,\\n  \\\"cohorts\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"prior-only\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 10,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0.75395542,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": 0.075395542,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": 0.6\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"trace-driven\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"local-history\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"unattributed\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 15,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 9,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0.48601148,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": 0.03240076533333333,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": 0.6\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"signals\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"graphNodes\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Entire graph nodes\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"filesTouched\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Predicted target files\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"issueLength\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Issue-text characters\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"filesNamed\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Path-like file mentions\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"traceReadback\\\": {\\n    \\\"retrievedAt\\\": \\\"2026-10-12T09:44:15.093Z\\\",\\n    \\\"matchedHistoryAttempts\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"verifiedWorkers\\\": 10,\\n    \\\"availableWorkerIds\\\": 10,\\n    \\\"historyWindowTruncated\\\": true,\\n    \\\"errors\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb647a50887d08e18aca4bc82804a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb65c970887d0a89c3fb824fea4df","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"The report now has the five-task plan table and pending A/B/C columns. I’m separating “history influenced routing” from “a learned cap was applied”: C can use observed pass rates before it has the five successful cost samples needed for a P90 cap, and the report will say so.\n","type":"output_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb65cb2e087d0af83f98b8e43a03b","role":"assistant","turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"revision":"retained_01a12fa8-62ea-73c2-beef-aca6620c3ef6"},"user_input_order":1612},"id":"msg_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb65cb2e087d0af83f98b8e43a03b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1791800924.714838,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_c71ff560daeb4c7fb6b60f169c7bb3b1","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb65ed27087d09f4074122c3d20db","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/evidence.ts\\n@@\\n-  if (selected?.includes('neatlogs:') \u0026\u0026 selected.includes('observed statistics') \u0026\u0026 selected.includes('P90')) return 'trace-driven';\\n+  if (selected?.includes('neatlogs:') \u0026\u0026 selected.includes('observed statistics')) return 'trace-driven';\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/evidence.test.ts\\n@@\\n-  it('requires the selected tier, not another candidate, to have trace-driven cap evidence', () =\u003e {\\n+  it('requires selected-tier observed trace statistics, not another candidate or a learned-cap claim', () =\u003e {\\n@@\\n-    expect(taskEvidence(run, [{ ...first, decision: `other neatlogs: 5 observations, observed statistics, P90; ${first.tier} neatlogs: 3 observations, observed statistics, config cap` }], 'fake')[0]?.cohort).toBe('unattributed');\\n+    expect(taskEvidence(run, [{ ...first, decision: `other neatlogs: 5 observations, observed statistics, P90; ${first.tier} neatlogs: 3 observations, observed statistics, config cap` }], 'fake')[0]?.cohort).toBe('trace-driven');\\n+    expect(taskEvidence(run, [{ ...first, decision: `other neatlogs: 5 observations, observed statistics, P90; ${first.tier} neatlogs: 1 observations, uses the prior, config cap` }], 'fake')[0]?.cohort).not.toBe('trace-driven');\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/scripts/routing-evidence.mjs\\n@@\\n-  'Prior-only requires an explicit prior statement for the chosen tier. Trace-driven requires explicit neatlogs provenance and an observed P90 cap for the chosen tier. Old ambiguous decisions are unattributed, not silently assigned to either group.', '',\\n+  'Prior-only requires an explicit prior statement for the chosen tier. Trace-driven requires explicit neatlogs provenance and observed statistics for the chosen tier; this can affect routing before five successful cost samples exist for a learned P90 cap. A configured cap is not a learned cap. Old ambiguous decisions are unattributed, not silently assigned to either group.', '',\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/README.md\\n@@\\n `runs.json` is a JSON array of paths containing `run.json` and `ledger.json`.\\n@@\\n tasks; missing baseline or v2 cohorts are reported as **not measured**.\\n+\\n+For the matched three-pass experiment, add `--comparison-dir \u003cfolder\u003e`.\\n+The folder contains `mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json` and, when results\\n+arrive, `comparison-passes.json`: an object mapping `A`, `B`, `C` to arrays of\\n+real run-directory paths (absolute or relative to that folder). A is top-tier\\n+baseline, B is Tally v1/priors, C is Tally v2/trace history. Missing passes stay\\n+pending. The report joins signals only at the exact pinned base SHA and task\\n+text, reports cost/verdict/attempts per task and per pass, and charts sizing\\n+against real costs with per-pass correlations. A pass C label does not itself\\n+prove that history influenced every route or that any cap was learned.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"node --input-type=module -e 'import {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from \\\"node:fs\\\"; const p=\\\"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/input-runs.json\\\"; const runs=JSON.parse(readFileSync(p,\\\"utf8\\\")); const path=\\\"/private/tmp/tally-cap-retry.Apm5J4/.tally/runs/run-20261012-100856Z\\\"; if(!runs.includes(path))runs.push(path); writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(runs,null,2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\");'\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Add only the newly authorized real cap-retry run to the generated audited input manifest, without modifying its run files.\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npm run build\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"node scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/input-runs.json --comparison-dir /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2 --issues /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/issues-current.json --out /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Regenerate the report with the real capped-stop/pass sequence while comparison passes remain explicitly pending.\",max_output_tokens:1500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npm test\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Test pinned-base comparison joins, explicit A/B/C assignments, missing results and existing behavior.\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800926.826191,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_c71ff560daeb4c7fb6b60f169c7bb3b1","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fa9-112b-7580-b76c-3001ddaf122b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791800971.563903,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 15.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"016c7f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"74fea4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.125092375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":15,\"output\":\"\\n\u003e tally-agents@0.1.0 build\\n\u003e tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"cf8437\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000525,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":578,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence\\\",\\n  \\\"runs\\\": 21,\\n  \\\"tasks\\\": 26,\\n  \\\"cohorts\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"prior-only\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 11,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 7,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0.94309226,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": 0.08573566,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": 0.6363636363636364\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"trace-driven\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"local-history\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"unattributed\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 15,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 9,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0.48601148,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": 0.03240076533333333,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": 0.6\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"cohort\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\\n      \\\"tasks\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"passed\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"errors\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"skipped\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"totalCostUsd\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"meanCostUsd\\\": null,\\n      \\\"successRate\\\": null\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"signals\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"graphNodes\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Entire graph nodes\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"filesTouched\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Predicted target files\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"issueLength\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Issue-text characters\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"filesNamed\\\",\\n      \\\"label\\\": \\\"Path-like file mentions\\\",\\n      \\\"n\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"pearson\\\": null,\\n      \\\"spearman\\\": null,\\n      \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"No estimable signal: fewer than 3 pairs or no variation.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"traceReadback\\\": {\\n    \\\"retrievedAt\\\": \\\"2026-10-12T09:44:15.093Z\\\",\\n    \\\"matchedHistoryAttempts\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"verifiedWorkers\\\": 10,\\n    \\\"availableWorkerIds\\\": 12,\\n    \\\"historyWindowTruncated\\\": true,\\n    \\\"errors\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e32f37\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.002028334,\"session_id\":60514,\"original_token_count\":31,\"output\":\"\\n\u003e tally-agents@0.1.0 test\\n\u003e vitest run\\n\\n\\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6a5cf9487d0a03f9bdab9b2e6ec","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6afd35c87d08fe6cdcae9a790c9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_d09ce9bc671f41e4a5b5b7ed9eb57f5c","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6affdf487d09efb173037979782","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,42p' /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md\",max_output_tokens:3200}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ao report --checkpoint --note 'Three-pass comparison report now loads lane A plan signals; A baseline/B priors/C trace-history columns are pending with no invented costs, dependency count for BENCH-1 remains unmeasured. Real cap retry included separately: stopped cheap $0.01956044 vs $0.018 cap, middle passed $0.16957640, total $0.18913684; classification ceiling/ledger remains ledger-derived. Input contract comparison-passes.json maps A/B/C to real run-directory arrays; exact base and text join guards. Implementation verification in progress.' --artifact /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Attach the newly requested three-pass report as soon as the durable output exists.\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:60514,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1300}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"node scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/input-runs.json --comparison-dir /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2 --issues /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/issues-current.json --out /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence --live-traces\",sandbox_permissions:\"require_escalated\",justification:\"Read-only verify stored worker traces including the new capped-stop/pass run, and refresh actual trace evidence; no trace exports or cfo.ai writes.\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1200}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791801008.0064774,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_d09ce9bc671f41e4a5b5b7ed9eb57f5c","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fa9-f30b-7381-bcdb-f7f8c3a58dc0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791801029.387674,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 10.7 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5f09e1\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":676,\"output\":\"# Routing evidence\\n\\nGenerated 2026-10-12T10:29:26.741Z. 21 closed real runs; 26 task outcomes (including skipped).\\n\\n## Three-Pass Comparison\\n\\nPlan measured 2026-10-12T09:30:21.074Z, pinned base 565e6ccd757ff794ead643dac7359efe67ec9db2. Signals source: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json.\\n\\n| Pass | Covered tasks | Task outcomes | Mean cost/task USD | Pass rate | Attempts |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n| A: top-tier baseline | 0/5 | 0 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| B: Tally v1 (priors) | 0/5 | 0 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| C: Tally v2 (trace history) | 0/5 | 0 | pending | pending | pending |\\n\\n| Task | Size | Targets | Dependents | Graph nodes | Text chars | Named paths | A: cost/verdict/attempts | B: cost/verdict/attempts | C: cost/verdict/attempts |\\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|\\n| BENCH-1 | small | 1 | unmeasured | unmeasured | 634 | 3 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| BENCH-2 | small | 2 | 26 | 12 | 746 | 2 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| BENCH-3 | medium | 4 | 70 | 23 | 869 | 3 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| BENCH-4 | medium | 3 | 35 | 21 | 803 | 3 | pending | pending | pending |\\n| BENCH-5 | large | 3 | 91 | 21 | 1110 | 4 | pending | pending | pending |\\n\\nPass labels are explicit experiment assignments, not proof that history affected every route in C. Actual routing provenance remains in tasks.csv. Costs only come from matching real ledgers; plan signals never supply spend. Missing passes/tasks stay pending; partial coverage is not a completed comparison. No savings claim before all three passes cover the same tasks. A single repeat establishes no statistical spread.\\n\\nComparison join exclusions: 0 (base/text/pass-label mismatches retained in results.json).\\n\\n## Before and after\\n\\n| Routing evidence | Task outcomes | Passed | Operational errors | Skipped | Mean cost (USD) | Pass rate |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n| prior-only | 11 | 7 | 4 | 0 | 0.08574 | 63.6% |\\n| trace-driven | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | not measured | not measured |\\n| local-history | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | not measured | not measured |\\n| unattributed | 15 | 9 | 4 | 0 | 0.03240 | 60.0% |\\n| baseline | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | not measured | not measured |\\n\\n![Estimated cost by routing](cost-by-routing.svg)\\n\\n![Success rate by routing](success-by-routing.svg)\\n\\nPrior-only requires an explicit prior statement for the chosen tier. Trace-driven requires explicit neatlogs provenance and observed statistics for the chosen tier; this can affect routing before five successful cost samples exist for a learned P90 cap. A configured cap is not a learned cap. Old ambiguous decisions are unattributed, not silently assigned to either group.\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"60e501\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a00345\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004541,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":50,\"output\":\"Preparing worktree (new branch 'worker-proof')\\n\\n Test Files  65 passed (65)\\n      Tests  797 passed (797)\\n   Start at  15:59:30\\n   Duration  11.54s (tests 81%, import 11%, transform 6%, setup 1%)\\n\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0260f2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.000867875,\"session_id\":34111,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6dfc8c487d085faaa0a768b5d23","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6efff0087d08221f43f4cd02bc8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_b50ebc7760984b34bdbeb30d44f17804","id":"ctc_0df8e55ea67e07bd016accb6f0295087d0bb450808c58a03d6","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/comparison-evidence.ts\\n@@\\n-        : row.query \u0026\u0026 task.impact?.query \u0026\u0026 task.impact.query !== row.query ? 'task text differs from the measured plan' : null;\\n+        : row.query \u0026\u0026 task.impact?.query !== row.query ? 'task text differs from the measured plan or is missing' : null;\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts\\n@@\\n-const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, mode: 'tally' as const, tasks: [{ ...run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!, impact: undefined }] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run', pass: 'B' as const };\\n+const impact = { source: 'entire-graph' as const, query: 'exact task text', nodes: [], edges: [],\\n+  totals: { filesTouched: 2, dependents: 26, testsPresent: true, nodes: 12, edges: 0 }, truncated: false };\\n+const input = { run: { ...run, baseCommit, mode: 'tally' as const, tasks: [{ ...run.tasks.find(task =\u003e task.taskId === taskId)!, impact }] }, ledger: [ledger[0]!], path: 'fake-run', pass: 'B' as const };\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/scripts/routing-evidence.mjs\\n@@\\n-await barChart('cost-by-routing.svg', 'Mean estimated list-price cost per task execution', 'meanCostUsd', value =\u003e `$${value.toFixed(4)}`);\\n+if (comparison) {\\n+  const average = outcomes =\u003e outcomes.length ? outcomes.reduce((sum, row) =\u003e sum + row.costNanos, 0) / outcomes.length / 1e9 : null;\\n+  const maximum = Math.max(...comparison.rows.flatMap(row =\u003e ['A', 'B', 'C'].map(pass =\u003e average(row[pass]) ?? 0)), 0.01);\\n+  const colors = { A: '#356bbb', B: '#ae4739', C: '#187d5b' };\\n+  const body = comparison.rows.map((row, index) =\u003e {\\n+    const y = 90 + index * 72;\\n+    return `\u003ctext x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"${y + 22}\\\"\u003e${escape(row.taskId)}\u003c/text\u003e` + ['A', 'B', 'C'].map((pass, p) =\u003e {\\n+      const value = average(row[pass]), yy = y + p * 19;\\n+      return `\u003ctext x=\\\"174\\\" y=\\\"${yy + 12}\\\"\u003e${pass}\u003c/text\u003e${value === null ? `\u003ctext x=\\\"220\\\" y=\\\"${yy + 12}\\\"\u003ePending\u003c/text\u003e`\\n+        : `\u003crect x=\\\"205\\\" y=\\\"${yy}\\\" width=\\\"${Math.max(1, value / maximum * 560)}\\\" height=\\\"13\\\" fill=\\\"${colors[pass]}\\\"/\u003e\u003ctext x=\\\"785\\\" y=\\\"${yy + 12}\\\"\u003e$${value.toFixed(5)} (n=${row[pass].length})\u003c/text\u003e`}`;\\n+    }).join('');\\n+  }).join('');\\n+  const height = 120 + comparison.rows.length * 72;\\n+  await writeFile(join(out, 'cost-by-routing.svg'), svg('Measured cost per task: A baseline, B priors, C trace history', height,\\n+    '\u003ctext x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"58\\\"\u003eA blue: top baseline; B red: Tally v1; C green: Tally v2. Mean across recorded outcomes.\u003c/text\u003e' + body\\n+    + `\u003ctext x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"${height - 15}\\\"\u003eUnstarted costs are not savings. Pending tasks are not zero-cost results; coverage is reported separately.\u003c/text\u003e`));\\n+} else await barChart('cost-by-routing.svg', 'Mean estimated list-price cost per task execution', 'meanCostUsd', value =\u003e `$${value.toFixed(4)}`);\\n@@\\n   ...comparison.rows.map(row =\u003e `| ${row.taskId} | ${row.size} | ${row.filesTouched} | ${row.dependents ?? 'unmeasured'} | ${row.graphNodes ?? 'unmeasured'} | ${row.issueLength} | ${row.filesNamed} | ${outcomeCell(row.A)} | ${outcomeCell(row.B)} | ${outcomeCell(row.C)} |`), '',\\n+  '![Cost per comparison task](cost-by-routing.svg)', '', '![Pass rate per comparison pass](success-by-routing.svg)', '',\\n@@\\n-  '![Estimated cost by routing](cost-by-routing.svg)', '', '![Success rate by routing](success-by-routing.svg)', '',\\n+  ...(!comparison ? ['![Estimated cost by routing](cost-by-routing.svg)', '', '![Success rate by routing](success-by-routing.svg)', ''] : []),\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npm run typecheck\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"npx vitest run agent/comparison-evidence.test.ts agent/evidence.test.ts\",max_output_tokens:1300}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:34111,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791801072.170857,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_b50ebc7760984b34bdbeb30d44f17804","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fab-0a72-7951-8663-4043bb571d08","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791801100.914707,"turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"64d5ba\",\"wall_t